\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Confirms It Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  In July\b0\par\par\uc2 142 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2009\par 14:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities didn't take any action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The MOF said it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from June 29 to July 29, as expected by market participants.\par \par \uc2 Japan has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since March 2004, when it abruptly ended a 15-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in which it sold Y35 trillion, mostly for dollars, in a bid to keep a stronger yen from snuffing out an economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data covered trades that are settled in July. Trades in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market are settled after two business days.\par \par \uc2 -Tokyo Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6895-7550\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2009 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020090731e57v006my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
