\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 934 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2009\par 11:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: EURO-ZONE CPI POSTS FIRST ANNUAL FALL ON RECORD \par Consumer prices in the 16 countries that use the euro fell on the year for the first time on record in June, the start of what the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has predicted will be a short period of deflation, final data showed Wednesday. (published 0902 GMT)  \par  \par  \par =BOJ EXTENDS LIQUIDITY STEPS, KEEPS KEY RATE UNCHANGED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan Wednesday kept its outlook for the nation's economy and prices largely unchanged from its semiannual report issued in April but extended temporary liquidity measures designed to aid corporate financing, showing the continued fragility of Japan's economy. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK JUNE CLAIMANT COUNT RISE SLOWEST FOR 13 MOS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The increase in the claimant count measure of U.K. unemployment rose at its slowest pace for 13 months in June, offering fresh evidence that the worst of the recession has past, official data showed Wednesday. (published 0839 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =CHINA INFLATION CONCERNS UP AS INFLOWS IMPROVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's broadest measure of money supply rose at its fastest pace in more than 12 years at the end of June, as the country posted the largest gain in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves since the global financial crisis hit and foreign direct investment into the country improved sharply. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =US LOCKE: FLEXIBLE CNY EXCHANGE RATE CAN AID RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A more flexible yuan exchange rate would accelerate the global economy's recovery, U.S. Commerce Secretary Gary Locke said Wednesday. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPE CAR MARKET IN JUNE +2.4%; INCENTIVES FUEL DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European new-car registrations in June rose 2.4% year-on-year, the first market increase in 14 months, as government-led scrapping incentives fueled demand in more than 10 countries. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRENCH MIN: NO NEED FOR SECOND ECONOMIC STIMULUS PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is no need for a second economic stimulus plan in France, but extra targeted measures haven't been ruled out, the minister for the plan, Patrick Devedjian, said Wednesday in a radio interview. (published 0847 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: ITALY JUN INFLATION SLOWS TO LOWEST RATE SINCE '68 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's consumer price index recorded its smallest increase in over 40 years, weighed by lower food and energy prices, data from Italian statistics office Istat confirmed Wednesday.(published 0808 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: SPAIN 2Q HOUSE PRICES -8.2% ON YR VS -6.5% IN 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish house prices posted their biggest decline in over 22 years in the second quarter of the year as home sales plummeted and builders tried to unload massive inventories accumulated during a decade-long housing boom. (published 0706 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA GOVT: UNLIKELY TO ACHIEVE $200 BLN FY EXPORT TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is unlikely to achieve its export target of $200 billion for the current fiscal year that started April 1 due to continuing global economic slowdown, the federal government said Wednesday. (published 0631 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA MINISTRY: EXTERNAL TRADE LIKELY TO KEEP FALLING IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Commerce Ministry spokesman Yao Jian said Wednesday that China's external trade is likely to continue falling in the third quarter, as trade figures were strong in the year-earlier period. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA JUNE LEADING ECON INDEX SHOWS SLOW RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian economic activity may have already passed its low point although a recovery in months ahead is likely to be very gradual, a private sector survey showed Wednesday. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RUSSIA MULLS USING WELFARE FUND TO COVER BUDGET GAP -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia is considering dipping into its oil fund set up to support the country's pension system to cover its budget deficit next year, the daily Vedomosti reports Wednesday. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =NZ FIN MIN SAYS NZD HIGHER THAN FUNDAMENTALS WARRANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Finance Minister Bill English Wednesday said the New Zealand dollar is higher than fundamentals warrant but that the government will not pursue policies to reduce the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the nation's export sector. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PBOC TO SELL CNY100B SPECIAL BILLS IN SEP - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to sell CNY100 billion worth of one-year special bills to selected banks in September, deploying a rarely used method to mop up excess liquidity and contain long-term inflation risks, bond traders told Dow Jones Newswires on Wednesday. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA JOBLESS RATE IN JUNE HIGHEST IN MORE THAN 8 YRS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's jobless rate rose to its highest level in more than eight years in June, official data showed Wednesday. And while economists say the jobs market may have hit bottom, any sustained recovery will be gradual. (published 0710 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: THE THREAT OF YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The threat of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains high, despite the return of the carry trade that helped to push the yen lower earlier this year. (published 0715 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: CAPPED NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Short- and long-end futures are all short-term capped now. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : EURO RISES VS YEN, DLR ON US EARNINGS OPTIMISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro rose against the yen and dollar in Asia Wednesday as another stronger-than-expected earnings announcement by a major U.S. firm encouraged Asian investors to buy riskier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: THE YEN WILL DEFLATE ITSELF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese yen is unlikely to stray into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  territory anytime soon, and will probably come down of its own accord anyway. (published 0042 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Katrina Bishop, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 207 842 9376; katrina.bishop@dowjones.com [ 15-07-09 0912GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090715e57f000eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
