\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Yen Spike A Temporary Threat To Japan Recovery\b0\par\par\uc2 By Riva Froymovich  \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN  \par \uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2009\par 20:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Just as the outlook for Japan's economy brightens, recovery is being threatened by a bout of yen strength.\par \par \uc2 But this is likely a short-term phenomenon that will reverse after the summer doldrums.\par \par \uc2 Japan's government raised its overall economic assessment for the third straight month Monday, in addition to its view on exports, as stimulus measures overseas are buoying demand for goods.\par \par \uc2 Recent trade data showed that exports increased in May for the third straight month, on a seasonally adjusted basis. And Japan's May industrial output rose 5.9% from a month earlier, the sharpest rise in more than half a century.\par \par \uc2 But a cheap yen is essential to support Japan's bread and butter - its export industries. Long-term yen strength at current levels will not be tolerated by policy makers, which traders by and large acknowledge, given \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's history of jawboning and market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 "If the yen's appreciation and stock declines last a long time, there are concerns that they may have a negative impact on both exporter and overall sentiment," which is a risk to the Japanese economy, said Economy Minister Yoshimasa Hayashi.\par \par \uc2 Japan is especially sensitive to dramatic moves in the yen speculative market, which last week saw "a massive net long addition" and a fall in shorts, noted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists at Scotia Capital.\par \par \uc2 However, while Hayashi had said last week the government needs to "keep monitoring moves" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said Monday that yen strength is connected to global concerns.\par \par \uc2 Hayashi was likely referring to the trend in which the yen advances in direct response to spikes in risk aversion, when traders sell higher-yielding assets and go into the lower-yielding, safer yen on global economic fears - something beyond the government's control.\par \par \uc2 This could be an indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has yet to reach levels of extreme concern and the current strain on the economy is not all that potent.\par \par \uc2 As a result, in the short term, the dollar could well test a break of Y90.0 before policy makers pipe up, say analysts.\par \par \uc2 Overnight, the dollar dropped to Y91.73, its lowest level since February, when the yen traded near its lowest levels since 1995.\par \par \uc2 "It's harder to justify a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government upgrading its economic forecast, particularly as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  deemed it unnecessary to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  back in January or February, said Cameron N. Umetsu, a senior economist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 He noted that in the last quarterly Tankan Survey of Japanese businesses, the average predicted exchange rate for the dollar was Y94.85. Among listed companies, the average forecast was closer to Y93.0 - close to recent trading levels, which means companies are prepared for now.\par \par \uc2 On Monday afternoon in New York, the dollar was at Y92.62 from Y92.39 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 This round of yen strength is likely tied to the break of important technical supports and option-related barriers, according to analysts at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Others add that the dip in oil prices may have also lent support to the yen's gains. The decline for oil led to an unwind in commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Australian dollar, where bets are often funded by the lower-yielding yen in a strategy called the carry trade.\par \par \uc2 "For that reason care should be used when interpreting the size of yen appreciation as telling us a lot about prospects in anything other than the short run," said \uc2 Barclays\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While global fears have indeed risen again following a period of high risk appetite in the second quarter of 2009, the world has recovered from the worst consequences of the \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  collapse, the analysts said.\par \par \uc2 (Riva Froymovich reports on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for Dow Jones Newswires in New York. The writer can be reached at 212-416-2217 or by e-mail: riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (Takashi Mochizuki in Tokyo contributed to this report.)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 13, 2009 14:18 ET (18:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090713e57d004e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
