\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2009\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YOSANO:NOT THINKING OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENING\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO WEAKEN YEN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday that he isn't planning to act to stop the yen's recent rise, prompting investors to lift the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a fresh two-month high against the dollar. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SUSPECTED TO HAVE BOUGHT DOLLAR - DEALERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is believed to have again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday morning to slow the baht's appreciation, mirroring action it had likely taken for most of this week, dealers said. (published 0154 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA MIN: EXPECT NO QUICK REBOUND IN DOMESTIC ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean economy isn't likely to recover anytime soon despite some positive signs in recent economic data, according to Minister of Knowledge Economy Lee Youn-ho. (published 0138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FED'S PLOSSER: WANTS ASSETS ON FED BALANCE SHEET TO BE SHORT TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve would be best restricting its asset purchases to the shortest possible maturities, to ease the process of its eventual withdrawal of life support from the financial markets, Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia President Charles Plosser said Thursday. (published 0113 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FED'S PLOSSER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NEEDS EXPLICIT INFLATION TARGETNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve needs stronger parameters, both on inflation and on its role independent from the U.S. government, a senior regional Fed official said Thursday. (published 2300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FED'S ROSENGREN: DEFLATION BIGGER CONCERN THAN INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The prospect of deflation is a bigger concern right now than inflation, despite the huge expansion of the Federal Reserve's balance sheet to combat the recession, Federal Reserve Bank of Boston President Eric Rosengren said Thursday. (published 0034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FED'S ROSENGREN: US IN 'A SEVERE RECESSION' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. economy is in a "severe recession" but could begin to grow by the end of the year if financial markets continue healing, a top Federal Reserve official said Thursday. (published 2341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE'S BLANCHFLOWER: HAVE PASSED MIDPOINT OF UK RECESSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. has passed the midpoint of its economic recession, although the outlook for the jobs market remains "terrible," a member of the Bank of England's Monetary Policy Committee said Thursday. (published 2230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =US RETAILERS FEAR NEW LAW COULD CURTAIL STORE CREDIT CARDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A new law governing credit card practices could make it harder for U.S. retailers to offer store-branded credit cards with perks aimed at closing the sale on big-ticket items. (published 2247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ:SCHWARZENEGGER PROPOSES BILLIONS IN NEW CALIF BUDGET CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 California Gov. Arnold Schwarzenegger on Tuesday proposed additional budget cuts to avoid some previously proposed borrowing. (published 2211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: SPEND IN HASTE, REPENT AT LEISURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The concerns of ratings agency \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  about the U.K.'s debt burden don't mean the country is on the cusp of losing its coveted AAA status, but they should serve as a warning to the leaders of key developed nations to think about the long-term repercussions of their current actions. (published 0007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DEALWATCH: FINCL SECTOR BANKERS CAN HELP RESOLVE PROVISIONING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial sector investment bankers must step in between auditors and politicians at odds over how banks account for allowances for loan losses. (published 2225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =GLOBAL YIELD: S&P WARNING TRAPS MAJOR ECONOMIES IN CATCH-22 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest warning Thursday from ratings firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  on the U.K.'s credit ratings sent a wake-up call to the governments of major economies: Get your fiscal house in order, or there could be a price to pay down the road. (published 1714 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: DOLLAR AT RISK AFTER STANDARD & POOR'S WARNS UK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fears over the U.S.'s deteriorating fiscal position and its impact on the dollar crystallized Thursday after the U.K. was warned that its easing measures - similar to those employed in the U.S. - could jeopardize its credit rating. (published 1740 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FED WATCH: IN SIGN OF TIMES, PRIMARY DEALER LIST SET TO GROW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After months of speculation, an early sign that more firms could be joining the dwindling list of primary dealers emerged Thursday. (published 1801 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 22-05-09 0200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090522e55m0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
