\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-GLOBAL MARKETS-Asia stocks rise on US bank optimism\b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Takes out incorrect references to MSCI ex Japan index rising for fourth straight day)\par \par \uc2 * Nikkei climbs 4 percent, led by exporters and banks\par \par \uc2 * Swiss franc stable after Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Berkshire, GE lose top credit rating\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Plumberg\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, March 13 (Reuters) - Asian stocks rose on Friday, with Japan's Nikkei up 4 percent, helped by a smaller-than-expected decline in U.S. retail sales and hopes that the largest U.S. banks will survive without a government takeover.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc was stable after notching up its biggest ever one-day drop against the euro on Thursday following news the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  sold francs in a bid to boost the economy, leaving some analysts wondering if this was the first shot in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war for trade competitiveness. [ID:nLB459488]\par \par \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2  told Reuters the bank does not need any more emergency cash from Washington and expects to stay private, while \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  said it was profitable in January and February, easing fears about further instability in the banking industry and sparking a rush back into equities.\par \par \uc2 "The economic situation seems to be better than what people were saying at the beginning of the year -- a view that has come about now that it seems that U.S. banks' earnings may not be atrocious," said Masaru Hamasaki, senior strategist at Toyota Asset Management in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Yet for every piece of news that improved investors' confidence, there was another that left questions about the sustainability of the market rebound.\par \par \uc2 For example, Wall Street chalked up its best three-day run since November after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  raised its outlook on \uc2 General Electric Co\uc2 's credit ratings to stable from negative, though it stripped the company of its "AAA" status. On the other hand, \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2  , Warren Buffet's conglomerate, lost its AAA rating and has a negative outlook from Fitch Ratings.[ID:nHKG147744]\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei <.N225> led the charge in Asia, climbing 4.5 percent, and was well on its way to the biggest weekly gain of the year. Shares of large Japanese banks were outperformers, with \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group\uc2  up 6.3 percent and \uc2 Mizuho Financial Group\uc2  rising 5.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI index of Asia Pacific stocks outside Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> rose 2.1 percent and hit its highest in about two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The materials and financial sectors were the biggest boosts.\par \par \uc2 BOLD SWISS MOVE\par \par \uc2 The euro was relatively unchanged on the day against the Swiss franc at 1.5327 francs <EURCHF=>, while the U.S. dollar was also steady at 1.1870 francs <CHF=>.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  stunned markets overnight with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Swiss franc as well as an interest rate cut as it forecast a deep recession. [ID:nLB459488]\par \par \uc2 The policy change was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by an advanced economy since the financial crisis broke out in the summer of 2007 and marked a new chapter in a global fight against deflation.\par \par \uc2 The move has also started a game of guessing who will follow the SNB's lead.\par \par \uc2 "The most obvious candidate for combining quantitative easing with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , simply because the BoJ has the historical precedent of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past," \uc2 UBS\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said in a note.\par \par \uc2 U.S. crude futures <CLc1> dipped back under $47 a barrel after rocketing 11 percent higher overnight following a not-so-dire U.S. retail sales report for February. Crude for April delivery slipped 0.5 percent to $46.77 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 1, CORRECTED)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|O|OIL|G|RNP|PGE|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090313e53d000a4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
