\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Strong Yen Poses Risks To Japan, But Not Dire Yet\b0\par\par\uc2 By Riva Froymovich   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 1,050 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2009\par 15:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The strong yen is clearly hurting Japan's economy and its businesses.\par \par \uc2 Yet the government will likely allow the yen's run of strength to continue in the near future as its effect isn't wholly negative. What's more, Japan isn't the only country grappling with market volatility, diminishing the success of any unilateral action.\par \par \uc2 The list of consequences from the yen's rise mounted this week: The Bank of Japan talked about deflation. December trade data showed a faster decline in exports, likely to hurt fourth quarter gross domestic product. \uc2 Sony Corp\uc2 . (SNE) said it would report an annual loss for the first time in 14 years. Japanese share prices have plummeted.\par \par \uc2 That list is likely to expand as the yen is seen advancing further against the euro and the dollar in the coming months, while the rest of the world feels the sweeping economic downturn. That's because Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considered a safe haven asset in times of high market uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 The yen rose Wednesday to a 13 1/2-year high versus the dollar and a seven-year high versus the euro. Many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts forecast the dollar will be between Y85.0 and Y80.0 by the end of March. Friday morning in New York, the dollar was at Y88.71 from Y88.78 Thursday, according to EBS, and from the Y100-area in October and November.\par \par \uc2 "As the recession gouges new depths in consumption, the lower the stock market goes, as any remaining confidence evaporates," said Andrew Wilkinson, senior market analyst at Interactive Brokers in Greenwich, Conn. "As that happens, investors look to the safety of the Japanese yen as a safe haven."\par \par \uc2 The dollar gains in the same waves of risk aversion as the yen, and U.S. businesses could see the same consequences.\par \par \uc2 However, a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has benefits for the domestic economy, analysts note.\par \par \uc2 Long-term valuations based on purchasing power parity indicate that the yen is fairly priced, said Benedikt Germanier, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in Stamford, Conn. And its higher value strengthens the purchasing power of Japanese consumers, a weak point in Japan's economy for some time.\par \par \uc2 In addition, a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes investing in Japan more attractive, particularly as capital preservation remains a key theme among investors.Japan wants capital coming into the country, Germanier said, citing recent government plans to scrap capital gains taxes on foreign investment to attract more investors.\par \par \uc2 Also, the effect of a more expensive yen on Japan's trade balance and its broader economy is not necessarily as negative as might be expected: For one, Japan's exports account for just 16% of gross domestic product, according to Haver Analytics, less than other countries such as Singapore, Hong Kong and Germany.\par \par \uc2 "Japan's export exposure is comparable with the U.K.," where exports account for 18% of GDP, said Germanier.\par \par \uc2 Naomi Fink, a Tokyo-based Japan strategist at The Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, added that looking at import and export prices overall, "we have palpable evidence that Japanese terms of trade have improved over the last five months."\par \par \uc2 Yen-based import prices have gone from a year-over-year expansion of 27.2% in August to a 22% year-over-year decline in December, while yen-based export prices have only fallen about 15% year-over-year, she noted.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Weak Global Demand At Heart Of Problem \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't be completely ruled out, many \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts are skeptical that it will act.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa on Friday expressed concerns about recent yen strength and domestic stock price weakness, and suggested dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is one option. However, Nakagawa's tone lacked any sense of urgency.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past to halt a sharp appreciation of the yen in times of heightened market volatility, last in March 2004. But \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Fink sees few incentives to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this time around.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For one, the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  based on actions in the past is enough to get yen bulls to exert caution. Second, low demand is at the heart of the matter for export weakness, more than yen appreciation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The "declines in the volume of exports have by far surpassed declines in their value, which shows that a weaker yen would prove a blunt tool in the face of falling external demand," she said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, a move to weaken the yen against its rivals would defeat the Bank of Japan's recent rate cut.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If "domestic investors were to go overseas for assets instead of buying debt issued to finance fiscal easing, BOJ cuts would have been all for naught," said Fink.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Also, an independent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seems less likely when other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs are also moving sharply. This week, the U.K. pound fell to a more than 23-year low versus the dollar. But a concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , such as in 2000, with the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Federal Reserve joining the BOJ, seems unlikely.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts add that sharp yen gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market have also been related to low levels of liquidity. Wednesday's sharp gains in the yen against the dollar were driven by the expiration of an option contract.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This "demonstrates that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are not working as usual. Had total sales amounted to $367 billion such a massive collapse would not have been possible," noted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Frankfurt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Riva Froymovich reports on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for Dow Jones Newswires in New York. The writer can be reached at 201-938-5063 or by e-mail: riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Takeshi Takeuchi in Tokyo contributed to this report.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We r