\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan steps up warning on markets, BOJ gloomy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano   \par \uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2009\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Japan stepped up its warning against financial market volatility but stopped short of saying Tokyo would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as persistent yen gains add to woes for the nation's export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2  In a sign of deepening problems, the Bank of Japan said on Friday financial conditions have become tighter even with its key policy rate near zero, suggesting that low rates alone may not be enough to pull Japan out of recession.\par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa said he was on high alert against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, as the yen hovered near its 13 \u189\'00\'BD   year high of 87.10 to the dollar hit earlier this week.\par \par \uc2  "We are watching financial markets very carefully and with a high sense of alert, and if necessary we must take prompt action in a broad sense," Nakagawa told a news conference.\par \par \uc2  While Japanese authorities have fired off similar volleys about recent yen rises, many market players expect them to stick to verbal warnings instead of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt yen gains, at least for now.\par \par \uc2  "If the dollar drops below 85 yen, or the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market shows sharp movement, caution about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase," said Kazuyuki Kato, treasury department manager at Mizuho Trust & Banking.\par \par \uc2  "But it is unlikely that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the current market levels." The yen stood around 88.50 to the dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2  Japan, like the United States, is in recession and can ill afford a rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which puts an extra choke-hold on exporters, who are already cutting jobs to cope with a global slump in demand.\par \par \uc2  The Nikkei share average fell to a two-month low after a massive loss warning from Sony Corp exacerbated concerns about corporate earnings and data showed further deterioration in the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2  The economic malaise in the United States and Europe is affecting Japan and Tokyo must act to keep the economy afloat, Nakagawa said, a day after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecast that Japan would plunge into its deepest contraction in modern times.\par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan on Thursday kept rates at 0.1 percent but said it would buy corporate bonds to ease a severe funding squeeze hurting the world's No. 2 economy, which it sees as sliding back into deflation for two years.\par \par \uc2  Sounding its bleakest note ever on the overall economy, the Bank of Japan said in a monthly report on Friday that it expected economic conditions to keep deteriorating for a while to come.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since March 2004, after a 15-month-long, 35 trillion yen ($394 billion) selling spree aimed at preventing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength from snuffing out an economic recovery.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  sets \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, deciding whether and when to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  implements it.\par \par \uc2  A finance spokesman for the main opposition party, Masaharu Nakagawa, also pitched in, telling Reuters a rising yen would damage \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be needed, although he added that caution is needed as buying dollars will increase holdings of U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2  Nakagawa's Democratic Party has a good chance of deposing Japan's long-ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) in an election this year, bringing an end to an almost unbroken run of LDP-led government going back more than half a century.  (Additional reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Writing by Leika Kihara; Editing by Hugh Lawson)    \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090123e51n0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
