\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Euro Rally Vs Dollar Comes To Abrupt End\b0\par\par\uc2 By Riva Froymovich   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2008\par 19:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The euro's dramatic rally versus the dollar is over, just days after \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders proclaimed the end of its autumn fall.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tug-of-war is a product of extremely thin year-end market conditions, which will continue through next week. These conditions were made worse after investors pulled out of positions over the last several months due to the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Not until January, when streams of liquidity reenter the market, will any definitive trend become clear. The euro may then be in for another leg down, as risk aversion remains high and global deleveraging into the dollar continues, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 Next week, speculative traders may be able to bully \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in either direction again, with most offices empty for traditional winter holidays. Markets around the world will largely be closed on Thursday, and many outside the U.S. will remain shut Friday.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, analysts say the euro may trade in a very wide range, between $1.35 to $1.45, but still below this week's heights. The euro reached a 12-week high of $1.4720 Thursday before declining 6.5% on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "Financial markets are notorious for their ability to overshoot," said Carl Forcheski, vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's advance versus the euro from August to November was very swift and due for a correction. But, the euro's sharp two-day gain, after the Federal Reserve surprised with a rate cut down to zero, should now correct back, he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has digested the Fed's maneuver and is back to focusing on euro zone economic weakness and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  negligence, compared with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolution.\par \par \uc2 "The ECB is being a little reluctant in monetary policy," said Forcheski, and this could lead to more economic turmoil. ECB members recently suggested that they may vote to keep rates on hold at the next meeting in January.\par \par \uc2 Next week, traders will pay attention to a speech from ECB chief Jean Claude Trichet on Tuesday and the release of the euro zone purchasing managers index later in the week.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar may climb back above Y90.0 in the coming week, a short-term bounce after an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warning from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, this advance won't likely hold for long as the yen has become a favorite safe-haven bet to escape the downturn in the U.S. and Europe.\par \par \uc2 Friday afternoon in New York, the euro was at $1.3846 from $1.4238 late Thursday, while the dollar was at Y89.57 from Y89.30. The euro was at Y124.00 from Y127.18. The U.K. pound was at $1.4860 from $1.5015, and the dollar was at CHF1.1119 from CHF1.0839 late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 (Riva Froymovich reports on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for Dow Jones Newswires in New York. The writer can be reached at 201-938-5063 or by e-mail: riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments [ 12-19-08 1356ET ]\par \par \uc2 1141   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020081219e4cj0003q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
