\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: BOJ Cuts Rates, Eases Liquidity To Tackle Slowdown\b0\par\par\uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2008\par 07:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan lowered interest rates Friday to support an economy that's increasingly feeling the pain of a global slump, becoming the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates to rock-bottom levels.\par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also announced several new steps to provide liquidity to capital markets, aiming to make it easier for cash-starved firms to raise funds.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ board voted 7-1 to cut the unsecured overnight call loan rate target to 0.1% from 0.30%. BOJ policy board member Tadao Noda voted against the decision.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ's move follows rate cuts by other major central banks in the face of a global financial crisis that shows little sign of abating. Tuesday, the Federal Open Market Committee cut its policy interest rate to a range of 0% to 0.25%. Central banks of the euro zone, the U.K. and Switzerland, among others, have also slashed rates in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Recent data showing Japan's economic outlook turning increasingly gloomy pushed the BOJ to lower rates. A downturn in exports has eaten into corporate profits, prodding firms to cut output and pushing up bankruptcies and unemployment. The yen's rise to a 13-year high against the dollar in recent days could worsen Japan's export performance.\par \par \uc2 The world financial crisis and domestic economic slump have caused Japanese business confidence to worsen at its sharpest pace since 1974, according to the BOJ's closely-watched tankan survey. And Japan's economy shrank by nearly 2% in annualized terms in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 Economic conditions "have been deteriorating and are likely to increase in severity for the immediate future," the BOJ statement said. "Given the slowdown in overseas economies and the turmoil in global financial markets, it will likely take some time" for Japan's economy to recover.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ "will continue to do its utmost...to facilitate the return of Japan's economy to a sustainable growth path with price stability," the bank said.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ also took several other steps to ease a logjam in corporate funding, noting that if financial conditions tighten, it could worsen the economic downturn.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ will step up its outright purchases of Japanese government bonds to Y1.4 trillion from Y1.2 trillion per month and will include new categories of bonds in its outright purchases, including 30-year, floating-rate and inflation-indexed JGBs.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ announced that a new facility accepting corporate debt as collateral for its lending \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which it announced Dec. 2 - will launch Jan. 8.\par \par \uc2 The bank also will begin, on a temporary basis, outright purchases of commercial paper and will investigate "how other corporate financing instruments may be employed."\par \par \uc2 In line with the overnight call rate cut, the Lombard lending rate, which is the rate that the BOJ charges for emergency loans, was lowered by 20 basis points to 0.30%.\par \par \uc2 The interest that the BOJ pays to banks keeping excess funds in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserve account was kept steady at 0.10%.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei 225 Stock Average briefly spiked on the decision but quickly fell back. JGBs soared, however, with lead March futures rising as high as 139.94, from 139.08 before the announcement, and the 10-year cash bond yield falling as low as 1.215%, a level it hasn't seen since 2005.\par \par \uc2 The moves were "aggressive but expected," \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  strategist Tatsuo Ichikawa said.\par \par \uc2 The surprising part, however, was that the bank decided not to choose just one or two of the policy options that had been suggested before the meeting, but to pursue all three simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 "They had to demonstrate that they've done all they can do," \uc2 Nikko Citigroup\uc2  JGB head trader Hideki Nakano said.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ could further expand the types of collateral it accepts, he said, "but otherwise they're pretty much done, except perhaps for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Statement: \par    \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boj.or.jp/en/type/release/adhoc/k081219.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boj.or.jp/en/type/release/adhoc/k081219.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tomoyuki Tachikawa, Megumi Fujikawa and Michael S. Arnold, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com, megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com, michael.arnold@dowjones.com. [ 19-12-08 0604GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081219e4cj0005c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
