\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Extends Overnight Bounce Above Y90.00\b0\par\par\uc2 By Riva Froymovich   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 17:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar extended overnight gains above Y90.00 Thursday morning in illiquid trading, after the dollar gained against the euro too.\par \par \uc2 It has since dipped back under that mark, although the dollar remains close.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday morning in New York, the euro was at $1.4287 from $1.4412 late Wednesday, while the dollar was at Y89.76 from Y87.40. The euro was at Y128.22 from Y125.78. The U.K. pound was at $1.5081 from $1.5508, and the dollar was at CHF1.0792 from CHF1.0747 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had hit an intraday high of Y90.01, just as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained against the euro following an announcement by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it reduced the rate of its deposit facility to 1.50% from 2.00%.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has been garnering support against the yen, though, since overnight trading after some cautionary words from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa Thursday said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a policy option, although he declined to comment on whether the government will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He said the ministry is keeping a close eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will take appropriate steps when they become necessary.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts say the MOF is probably uneasy with the yen's new strength. The analysts are wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar has been selling off against the yen, considered a safe haven, for several weeks. The pace picked up last week, with growing fears on the U.S. economy, and hastened after the Federal Open Market Committee slashed interest rates more than expected Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a 13-year low of Y87.13 Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 -By Riva Froymovich, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938-5063; riva.froymovich@dowjones.com [ 12-18-08 1202ET ]\par \par \uc2 1074 1158 1863 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020081218e4ci0003m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
