\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-TOPWRAP 1-Japan seen cutting rates, OPEC cuts don't lift oil\b0\par\par\uc2 845 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Japan seen cutting rock-bottom interest rates further\par \par \uc2 * OPEC output cuts fail to lift oil prices\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  warns of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * BOE's Bean says zero rates possible in Britain too (For full crisis coverage, double click on [nCRISIS]\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 18 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Thursday poised to drive rates close to zero to help the economy hit hard by crumbling global demand, a decline underscored when OPEC's biggest ever supply cut failed to lift oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan is expected to cut interest rates from already rock-bottom 0.3 percent on Friday after the U.S. Federal Reserve's dramatic rate cut, but stop short -- for now -- of reviving a policy of flooding markets with massive amounts of cash.\par \par \uc2 The Fed slashed U.S. rates to 0-0.25 percent, pushing the dollar down to a 13-year low near 87 yen <JPY=> on Wednesday and adding pressure on Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to join another round of rate cuts when its policy meeting ends on Friday. [ID:nT222002]\par \par \uc2 The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also expected to leap into action on Thursday, possibly trimming rates by half a percentage point to help spur economic growth [ID:nMAN238761]\par \par \uc2 The severity of the global economic downturn sparked by the U.S. mortgage market meltdown last year prompted policymakers to look for unconventional tools after many have already slashed rates to historic lows and rushed out massive stimulus packages.\par \par \uc2 Bank of England Deputy Governor Charles Bean said in an interview with the Financial Times zero rates were also a possibility in Britain, on its way to its first recession since 1990s. [ID:nLI001633]\par \par \uc2 After a recent string of gloomy data, Japan's government was set to downgrade its assessment of the recession-hit economy in December, the Nikkei newspaper reported.\par \par \uc2 "If the BOJ shares the government's view on the financial situation, I expect the bank to take whatever steps are necessary," Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities also warned of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a surge in the yen, battering exporters, such as carmakers, already hit by collapsing global demand.\par \par \uc2 "We'll deal appropriately with it including \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Chief Cabinet Secretary Takeo Kawamura told a news conference [ID:TKF003216].\par \par \uc2 SUDDEN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOVES\par \par \uc2 In a sign of the worsening woes, the head of Japan's auto industry lobby said that the yen's current strength would have a profound negative impact on domestic carmakers, saying he hoped \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would return to stability.\par \par \uc2 "Sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, especially big ones, will not only hurt short-term corporate profitability but also make it very difficult for companies to make medium to long-term plans," Satoshi Aoki, chairman of the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association, told a news conference [ID:nTKG003154]\par \par \uc2 Japanese demand for new vehicles will likely fall 4.9 percent in 2009, the group said, predicting the first drop below 5 million vehicles in 31 years.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was hovering at around 87.75 yen <JPY=> off its 13-year low and touched a 2-1/2-month low against the euro as the U.S. rate cut widened the interest rate differential in favour of the euro zone \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Expectations that the Bank of Japan and other central banks in the region will follow the Fed's lead and drive borrowing costs near record lows lifted bank shares in Tokyo and helped most stock markets in the region clock up moderate gains.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Nikkei average <.N225> closed 0.6 percent higher and the MSCI index of stocks in Asia-Pacific outside Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> was up 1.3 percent by 0630 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices <CLc1> steadied at around $40 a barrel on Thursday, near its lowest in more than four years, a sign that slowing demand was trumping OPEC's biggest-ever production cut.\par \par \uc2 The Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC), keen to build a floor under dipping prices, announced on Wednesday it would cut 2.2 million barrels daily of output starting Jan. 1, slightly more than expected.\par \par \uc2 "The world economy is driving the price more than anything OPEC can do at this state," said Gary Ross, CEP of consultancy PIRA Energy. "It will be hard for the cuts to have any traction with regard to price in a deteriorating economic environment."\par \par \uc2 South Korea, one of Asian economies hardest hit by the global financial crisis, said on Thursday it would launch a 20 trillion won ($15.1 billion) fund in January to help banks replenish capital and encourage them to lend.\par \par \uc2 In Germany, the country's leading think tank Ifo is expected to announce another drop in its closely-watched business climate index after it hit a 16-year low last month. (Additional reporting by Reuters bureaus worldwide; Writing by Linda Sieg; Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL/ (TOPWRAP 1, REPEAT)|LANGEN|Z|AUF|SI|SNI|IF|PHD|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081218e4ci000cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
