\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Recent comments by policy makers on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the financial crisis click [ID:nCRISIS])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The yen's surge to a 13-year high against the dollar after the U.S. Federal Reserve slashed interest rates this week has prompted concerns that the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could push Japan into a deeper recession.\par \par \uc2 A stronger yen makes Japanese goods less competitive overseas and deflates earnings made abroad when repatriated, hurting Japan's export-dependent economy.\par \par \uc2 Government data up to the end of November showed that Japanese monetary authorities have not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 2004, when they had spent some 30 trillion yen ($342 billion) to stem a sharp appreciation of the yen.\par \par \uc2 However, Japanese officials have recently expressed concern over the impact of the yen's strength. Any market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be conducted mainly by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  under direction from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which decides on Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Following are recent comments of Japanese policy makers and a former finance ministry official on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets:\par \par \uc2 CHIEF CABINET SECRETARY TAKEO KAWAMURA, Dec 18, in news conference:\par \par \uc2 "We'll deal appropriately with it, including (the option of) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 VICE FINANCE MINISTER FOR INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS NAOYUKI SHINOHARA, Dec 18, speaking to reporters:\par \par \uc2 "We will take appropriate actions as needed." CHIEF CABINET SECRETARY TAKEO KAWAMURA, Dec 17, in news conference:\par \par \uc2 "The abnormal rise in the yen could affect export industries and I hope that the BOJ will make a comprehensive consideration, including those factors to decide its monetary policy."\par \par \uc2 BANK OF JAPAN GOVERNOR MASAAKI SHIRAKAWA, Dec 15, in interview with the Financial Times:\par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy does not just focus on exchange rates. Our general stance is to assess overall economic conditions and we don't think about the effect of exchange rates as an isolated factor: everything affects the economy."\par \par \uc2 "It is not appropriate to frame the discussion as if we can manipulate or control the level of the exchange rate. Of course, monetary policy affects exchange rates indirectly, but there is no one-to-one correspondence."\par \par \uc2 "At the end of the day, the exchange rate is determined by market forces."\par \par \uc2 FINANCE MINISTER SHOICHI NAKAGAWA, Dec 12, in news conference:\par \par \uc2 Asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets: "It is not in my head at all at this moment."\par \par \uc2 BOJ GOVERNOR SHIRAKAWA, Dec 10, at parliament committee:\par \par \uc2 "As a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we will implement monetary policy by examining how \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves could affect the economy." He also said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  had the option of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were big.\par \par \uc2 FINANCE MINISTER NAKAGAWA, NOV 21, speaking to foreign journalists:\par \par \uc2 "We must act firmly on extreme moves in the markets."\par \par \uc2 FINANCE MINISTER NAKAGAWA, Nov 13, at parliament committee:\par \par \uc2 "Rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate swings would have a negative impact on the economy." He also said rapid moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates need to be avoided at all cost.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE FINANCE MINISTER FOR INTERNATIONAL AFFAIRS HIROSHI WATANABE, Nov 4, in interview with Reuters:\par \par \uc2 "I don't think dollar-yen levels of 80-85 yen, or even 90 yen, would last too long," citing Japan's weak economic outlook as a reason.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels aside, authorities need to act when they feel exchange-rates would move further and deeper at a certain direction. If they don't feel that way, they don't need to act."\par \par \uc2 FINANCE MINISTER NAKAGAWA, Oct 31, in meeting with media:\par \par \uc2 Asked about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets: "I have many things in my pocket, but I won't comment on whether I will use them or when I would use them."\par \par \uc2 The Group of Seven industrialised nations issued on Oct 27 an emergency statement expressing concerns about excessive volatility of the yen.\par \par \uc2 PRIME MINISTER TARO ASO, Oct 24, speaking to reporters ahead of ASEM meeting in Beijing:\par \par \uc2 "As I have been saying, I don't have any intention to fret over rapid fluctuations in stocks and the dollar. But what could affect the real economy most are such rapid moves."\par \par \uc2 CHIEF CABINET SECRETARY KAWAMURA, Oct 23, in news conference:\par \par \uc2 "The yen's rise may bring some benefits but we need to pay attention to how it will affect the real economy through exports and imports." (Reporting by Tokyo Economic Policy Desk)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL/JAPAN-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081218e4ci0006f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
