\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar jumps vs yen as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  risk mounts\b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 01:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar posts biggest one-day gain vs yen in over a month\par \par \uc2 * Japanese finance minister says \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an option\par \par \uc2 * Dollar rebounds from near 3-month low vs euro\par \par \uc2 * BoJ seen to cut rates Friday following Fed's move (Adds comments, updates prices; changes byline)\par \par \uc2 By Vivianne Rodrigues\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar posted its biggest one-day rise against the yen in more than a month Thursday as speculation mounted that the Japanese government may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also rose against the euro as some investors took profits after the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp gains in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 The yen fell a day after hitting its highest level in more than 13 years after Japanese authorities stepped up their rhetoric against a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is hurting the nation's exporters.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa said on Thursday he is watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "with a sense of urgency." He refrained from commenting on whether the ministry would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but added that it has the option to do so.\par \par \uc2 "We saw a reversal in dollar/yen based on the rising risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Vassili Serebriakov, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  in New York. "If the yen were to strengthen again, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be very possible.\par \par \uc2 "It will certainly slow down the yen's advance," he added.\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading in New York, the dollar rose 2.3 percent to 89.29 yen, after hitting a session high at 90.02 yen. The dollar fell to 87.11 on Wednesday, the lowest level in more than 13 years.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan will announce its interest-rate decision at the end of its two-day policy meeting on Friday, and analysts said the Federal Reserve's aggressive rate cut on Tuesday has raised pressure on the BoJ to cut rates.\par \par \uc2 Two-thirds of economists polled by Reuters this week expect the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates from the current 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 EURO ADVANCE STALLS\par \par \uc2 The dollar rebounded from a nearly three-month low against the euro after the greenback sold off sharply following the Fed's rate decision on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "The moves that we saw (in the dollar) since the Fed's rate decision were fairly dramatic so we wouldn't be surprised to see some corrective pullback at this stage," said Serebriakov at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro last traded down 1.2 percent at $1.4236. The euro had earlier risen to $1.4719, the highest level since Sept. 25.\par \par \uc2 Adding to pressure on the euro was an announcement from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it would widen its interest- rate corridor and cut the return it gives banks for holding cash at the bank.\par \par \uc2 The rate of the deposit facility will be reduced from 50 to 100 basis points below the rate of the main refinancing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bank said.\par \par \uc2 In addition, analysts said the euro's latest rise may also give the ECB room to cut interest rates again next month rather than stand pat as some in the market are expecting.\par \par \uc2 "The strength of the euro could cause the ECB to change its stance on keeping rates steady because recent euro gains are really the same as a tightening of policy," said Kathy Lien, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at GFT \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Declines in the dollar gained momentum earlier this week after the Fed's big rate cut tilted the yield differential in favor of the single euro-zone \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Additional reporting by Wanfeng Zhou and Steven C. Johnson in New York; Editing by Jan Paschal)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 8)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081218e4ci00022\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
