\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,119 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN '09 AUTO SALES EXPECTED TO FALL TO 31-YEAR LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Domestic auto sales in Japan are expected to drop to their lowest level in 31 years in 2009 as the global economic slowdown dents consumer spending, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association said Thursday. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO LAUNCH KRW20T FUND TO HELP BANKS RAISE CAPITAL BASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government plans to launch a KRW20 trillion fund in January to help local banks raise their capital base and access cash whenever needed until the end of 2009, the Financial Services Commission said Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN BKS WARN ON ESCALATING LOAN LOSSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More of Australia's major banks warned Thursday that bad loans will rise and loan growth is likely to slow as the impact of the global financial crisis hits home. (published 0529 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NZ TSY SEES BIGGER NZ BUDGET DEFICITS, LOW GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand Treasury said Thursday the government's budget position and the country's growth outlook had deteriorated significantly due to a worsening international outlook, and signaled a spike in the government's borrowings. (published 2348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA WPI +6.84% ON YR IN WEEK ENDED DEC 6 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation rate eased to 6.84% in the week ended Dec. 6 from 8.00% in the previous week, the government said Thursday. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S AOFM CALLS FOR MORE RMBS TRANSACTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian Office of Financial Management Thursday said it is likely to issue four new mandates to purchase residential mortgage-backed securities from issuers in its second mandate selection round. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: DEMAND IN 2-YR JGB AUCTION FIRM; BOJ EXPECTED TO CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Demand for two-year Japanese government bonds was firm at Thursday's auction, as growing speculation that the Bank of Japan will cut interest rates Friday drives down short-term interest rates. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA EXPECTS TO ISSUE MEDIUM-TERM NOTES AFTER JAN-OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia expects to issue medium-term notes after January, a government official said Thursday. (published 0112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ DEC BUSINESS CONFIDENCE DEPRESSED, ECON IN STRIFE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand business confidence in December remained in deeply pessimistic territory despite a modest bounce, as the worsening outlook for the global and domestic economies brought firms to their knees. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  KAWAMURA:TO ACT SUITABLY ON YEN, INCLUDING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's chief government spokesman said Thursday the government will take appropriate steps as needed, including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , to respond to the yen's sharp rise. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NAKAGAWA: NO COMMENT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa on Thursday declined to comment on whether the government is considering \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, but he added he will take appropriate steps when necessary. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA SELLS HK$1.94 BLN IN NEW YORK WED TO DEFEND US DLR PEG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday it sold HK$1.94 billion during the New York trading session Wednesday to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. (published 0017 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: DOLLAR GOING BELOW KRW1,300 "NOT SURPRISING" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar's fall Thursday below KRW1,300 isn't surprising when economic fundamentals are taken into account, a senior official at South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance said. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI PM:TO STICK WITH PLAN FOR ADDITIONAL BUDGET DEFICIT 09 FY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's newly appointed prime minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said Thursday that his government will stick with the previous administration's plan that envisaged an additional budget deficit of THB100 billion in the current fiscal year. (published 0219 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: WORLD BANK WORKING TO ENSURE FINANCING FOR INDONESIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The World Bank has been working with Australia, Japan and the Asian Development Bank to help Indonesia finance its budget deficit, World Bank President Robert Zoellick said Thursday. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: THAI PM: ECON TO SLOW; FORESEE UNEMPLOYMENT WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's newly appointed Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said Thursday he expects the country's economy to slow and unemployment to worsen. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S:LIQUIDITY CONSTRAINTS HIT NON-US REGIONAL,LOCAL GOVTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Non-U.S. regional and local governments, or RLGs, have all been affected to varying degrees by liquidity constraints and market access restrictions, and this is likely to continue in 2009, said ratings agency Moody's Investors Service Inc. in a report Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:CANADA FIN MIN SAYS GDP TO SHRINK, BUDGET DEFICIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian Finance Minister Jim Flaherty said Wednesday the outlook for the economy has become much grimmer han just a month ago as the U.S. recession deepens and prices for many of the commodities Canada produces, especially oil, decline. (published 2245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SCUFFLES IN S KOREA PARLIAMENT OVER BID TO PASS TRADE PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL --South Korean lawmakers barricaded themselves into a parliamentary committee room Thursday after opponents smashed down the door, as tempers flared over a bid to ratify a U.S. free trade pact. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: FED'S NEW PLAN CARRIES RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve has exhausted the full might of its central monetary policy tool and is now resorting to unorthodox measures to get the U.S. economy going again. (published 2127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =RATE FUTURES REPORT: YIELD GRAB, FED TSY BUY HOPES LIFT MKT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prices continued to soar Wednesday for long-term Treasury futures, as traders grabbed any yield they could in a record low interest rate environment. (published 2116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DERIVATIVES DIARY: IT'S NOT CURTAINS FOR FED FUNDS FUTURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For fed-funds futures traders, the world changed Tuesday, with the Federal Reserve's historic decision to shift away from interest rates as its primary tool for monetary policy. (published 2107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FED WATCH: MATCHING FUNDS RATE TO REALITY WITH RATE RANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve Board's switch from a target interest rate to a rate range is an admission it can no longer control the level at which the federal-funds rate trades. (published 2133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FOCUS: NZ ECON ILLS MAY PROLONG, DELIVER NASTY SIDE EFFECTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's recession is set to extend well into next year despite deep interest rate cuts, while large fiscal stimulus in the works could have nasty side effects, analysts say. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =NZ GOVT MASSIVE BOND ROLLOUT LIKELY A TOUGH SELL - ANALYSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's Debt Management Office will have a tough time selling its massive volume of government bonds, and will have to settle for lower premiums to dispose of stock, analysts say. (published 0412 GMT) [ 18-12-08 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081218e4ci0006p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
