\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -US dollar tumbles after Fed cuts rates to record low\b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2008\par 01:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * US dollar tumbles versus euro, yen after Fed rate cut\par \par \uc2 * Fed cuts rates more than expected to record low\par \par \uc2 * Fed says may keep rates at "exceptionally low levels"\par \par \uc2 * Yen nears 13-year high; boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talks\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Vivianne Rodrigues\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar tumbled versus the euro and the yen Tuesday after the Federal Reserve cut its benchmark interest rates more than expected to a record low, further diminishing the appeal of the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The Fed cut its federal funds rate target to a range of zero to 0.25 percent from the previous target of 1.0 percent, and said it would use "all available tools" to dispel a year-long recession.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets had expected the Fed to lower rates by no more than three-quarters of a point.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar is falling against all major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... because it was a larger-than-expected cut," said Matt Esteve, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Tempus Consulting in Washington.\par \par \uc2 "On one side, we effectively have a zero interest rate in the U.S., and on the other side, the Fed has sent a sign that they are ready to use all tools to help the U.S. economy out of recession," he added.\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading in New York, the euro was up about 3.0 percent at $1.4099, a 2 1/2-month high. It traded as high as $1.4144, more than five cents above its session trough of $1.3631.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar had its biggest daily decline against the Swiss franc since 1995. It last traded 3.2 percent lower against the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.1205 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Versus the yen, the dollar was down 1.6 percent to 89.06, within a striking distance to a 13-year low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Fed's rate cut pushed the fed funds target to its lowest level on record, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would keep it at "exceptionally low levels for some time."\par \par \uc2 The surprise move put the Fed in unprecedented policy territory, but analysts mostly approved of the move.\par \par \uc2 "It's a highly unorthodox and creative step," said Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 The Bank of New York\uc2  Mellon in New York. "We think it's the best possible move for the U.S. consumer and for the financial market."\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks rallied after the announcement, while the InterContinental Exchange's U.S. dollar index, which tracks the value of the greenback against a basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell 1.8 percent to 80.628.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's rate cut move is "an incredibly strong public declaration that the Fed will throw everything it has in attempting to stabilize the financial and economic situation," Mohamed El-Erian, the chief executive of bond giant \uc2 Pacific Investment Management Co\uc2 , told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "After this 'wow' statement, there should be no question about policy willingness," he added.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar also tumbled against the Australian and New Zealand dollars in a sign the Fed's move may be positive for risk appetite and riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 GOLDMAN SACHS, BANK OF JAPAN\par \par \uc2 Demand for the greenback started to dwindle earlier in the session as investors cut their exposure to risk after \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  posted its first loss as a public company.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's sharp drop in recent days in particular against the yen has raised speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength as it nears a 13-year high.\par \par \uc2 U.S. data released earlier on Tuesday showed new housing starts and permits plunged to record lows in November, while consumer prices dropped at a record rate for a second straight month.\par \par \uc2 Analysts and fund managers said the very soft readings on inflation and continued deterioration in the housing sector support views of a very expansionary policy stance.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Steven C. Johnson, Wanfeng Zhou and Jennifer Ablan in New York;)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 8)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081216e4cg0002c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
