\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-SNAP ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  would slow, not stop, yen rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eric Burroughs and Masayuki Kitano   \par \uc2 876 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2008\par 09:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to correct the day of the week in paragraph 1)\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG/TOKYO, Dec 12 (Reuters) - The dollar's tumble to a 13-year low below 90 yen <JPY=> on Friday after the U.S. automaker rescue plan died in Congress stirred speculation that Japanese authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's surge.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe that while \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shied away from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for nearly five years, the hit to its big manufacturers -- the economy's mainstay -- from a stronger yen has made them more willing to act.\par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Naoyuki Shinohara, told Reuters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act appropriately depending on the market situation -- a clear warning that authorities are prepared to sell the yen. [ID:nTKU003237]\par \par \uc2 But media quoted Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa as saying that the ministry was not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market now. [ID:nTKF003205] Nakagawa will hold a news conference from 0940 GMT on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The MOF makes decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are then conducted by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GAUGING SUCCESS\par \par \uc2 For \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely be considered successful even if it simply slowed the yen's rise rather than stopped it altogether.\par \par \uc2 Japan has a long history of trying to stem yen strength by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars, but it has stayed out of the market since a 35 trillion yen ($382 billion) campaign over 15 months ended in March 2004.\par \par \uc2 The MOF has gradually moved away from heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because that last campaign had mixed results, with the yen steadily rising the whole time to near 103.40 to the dollar in the last month.\par \par \uc2 The explosion of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading also means Japan may have a harder time trying to have much impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Daily turnover in the dollar/yen exchange rate averaged $397 billion in 2007, a nearly 40 percent increase in six years, according to the last survey of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the Bank for International Settlements.\par \par \uc2 Japan does risk having market players try to test its will and ability to prevent further yen strength if it does \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may even face a situation of fighting against its own investors if yen strength starts to happen due to Japanese investors repatriating some of their massive investments abroad.\par \par \uc2 So far Japanese investors have defied expectations and kept shifting money into foreign assets during the turmoil of the past few months.\par \par \uc2 And if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is likely to go it alone.\par \par \uc2 While Group of Seven economic powers issued a rare statement singling out the volatile yen in October, the move came at the request of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and French Economics Minister Christine Lagarde later said any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be conducted by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone.\par \par \uc2 PSYCHOLOGICAL EFFECT\par \par \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the yen will likely attempt to have a psychological impact on the market even while battling what has been a very painful hit to the country's huge exporters.\par \par \uc2 Sony\uc2 's decision this week to lay off 16,000 workers and cut $1.1 billion of costs serves as a reflection of how Japan's big companies are suffering from the global economy's slide into recession.\par \par \uc2 The Reuters Tankan, which serves as a leading indicator of the BOJ's quarterly survey of sentiment at big manufacturers, plunged at a record pace in November. [JP/TAN1]\par \par \uc2 The BOJ's tankan will be released on Monday, and in the previous edition in September big manufacturers had assumed a dollar/yen exchange rate 102.48 -- a full 14 percent above current levels near 89.70.\par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a low of 88.10 yen on Friday, the lowest since 1995 and raising the prospect of a drop near the all-time low of 79.75 touched that year. [FRX/]\par \par \uc2 FIGHTING DERIVATIVES FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials are also likely worried that a further dollar plunge against the yen would trigger more exotic derivatives that have added fuel to the yen's surge and the sell-off in the Nikkei and other markets this year.\par \par \uc2 The derivatives, including some such as power-reverse dual-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes, were a popular form of the carry trade among Japanese individual investors and involved options in dollar/yen and other yen crosses.\par \par \uc2 The options are placed at levels like 90 and 80 in dollar/yen and used as a way to boost the relatively high yields the derivatives offer.\par \par \uc2 But when the options are triggered, the hedging flows for banks that had sold the structures force them to sell the dollar into a falling market.\par \par \uc2 Such forced selling tied to exotic derivatives played a role in the yen's 10.3 percent surge on the BOJ's trade-weighted index in October -- the biggest since the yen was allowed to trade freely in 1973.\par \par \uc2 That monthly spike also eclipsed previous milestones in the yen's history, such as its surge when carry trades were unwound en masse in 1998 and in 1985 when G5 powers agreed on the Plaza Accord to depreciate the dollar against the yen.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /YEN (SNAP ANALYSIS) (CORRECTED)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081215e4cc000kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
