\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: December A Curse For Dlr, Selling Ahead\b0\par\par\uc2 1,008 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2008\par 22:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds latest net short position on euro-dollar in eighth paragraph; updates \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotes.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Min Zeng \par    A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--There is likely to be no "Happy Winter Holiday" greeting for the U.S. dollar for the rest of December trading.\par \par \uc2 Market participants said more dollar selling is in the cards through year end, especially against European rivals such as the euro. That will be quite a reversal of the steep rally over the past few months.\par \par \uc2 The repatriation among U.S. investors from foreign assets such as equities has been waning. In contrast, foreign companies are expected to sell the dollar and repatriate money to window-dress their balance books at year end.\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve's pumping of liquidity to ease stress in money markets also flooded dollars into the global system, easing the dollar shortage from the credit crunch following the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  in mid-September, and reducing demand for the greenback.\par \par \uc2 More dollars are going to be ushered into the system next week as financial markets widely expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut the 1% federal-funds target rate by as much as 75 basis points. There is rising speculation that the Fed may suggest keeping rates low for a long period of time while adopting other unconventional methods to stimulate growth.\par \par \uc2 "The Fed is basically dropping dollars from helicopters," said Tom Fitzpatrick, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Citigroup Global Markets Inc\uc2 . in New York. "It certainly creates enough momentum for a correction for the dollar move. It is quite feasible that we could see more correction" to push the dollar down a bit further against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Seasonal factors also work against the dollar. Robert Sinche, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Bank of America Corp\uc2 . in New York, said that the dollar tends to weaken against the euro in December. He noted that for each last week of December from 2000 to 2007, speculative investors such as hedge funds have been net long the euro. A long position is a bet on a rise in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  relative to its peers, while a short is the opposite.\par \par \uc2 Citing data from the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission, Sinche said the average position for euro-dollar has been a net long of about 29,000 contracts. As of Dec. 9, the speculative market still had a short euro-dollar position of 16,668 contracts, according to data released from CFTC Friday afternoon, signaling more buying of euros later this month.\par \par \uc2 'Soft Underpinning' For Dollar\par \par \uc2 "There is a soft underpinning for the dollar," said Sinche, saying that the weakness of the dollar against the euro is likely to continue into early next year. He expected the euro to rise above $1.4 during the first quarter of next year, though that is still below the record high above $1.6 hit in July.\par \par \uc2 Friday afternoon in New York, the euro was at $1.3386, up from $1.3339 Thursday, according to EBS. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched a high of $1.3416 earlier Friday, its strongest level against the dollar in almost eight weeks. Against the yen, the euro traded at Y121.73, down from Y122.44.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at Y90.98, down from Y91.80 late Thursday, after touching Y88.10, the lowest level since August 1995. The pound was at $1.4982, down from $1.5003. The dollar was at CHF1.1755, down from CHF1.1848. The euro hit a record high against the pound of GBP0.8996 and recently traded at GBP0.8931.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the euro-dollar is expected to trade between $1.32 and $1.37 next week, while the dollar-yen will be between Y88 and Y94.\par \par \uc2 Benedikt Germanier, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS AG in Stamford, Conn., said the dollar may weaken further against the yen in the coming week, retesting the low of Y88.10 with a potential fall to Y85. Germanier said the ongoing financial and economic stress will keep the yen supported.\par \par \uc2 The yen has rallied this year against major rivals like the dollar, the euro, the pound and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Australia, New Zealand and Canada, amid risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 Investors sold higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world to repay yen-denominated loans used to finance the investments. Japan's ultra-low interest rate has pushed global investors to borrow the yen to seek higher returns in assets elsewhere. But as risk aversion returns, investors unwind the so-called yen-based carry trade, boosting demand for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sharp rise in the yen has raised worries that Japanese officials may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to damp its appreciation against the dollar because a rising yen makes Japanese exports less competitive in the global markets. Japan's economy has entered into recession with exports plunging. The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the first quarter of 2004.\par \par \uc2 Market participants generally said that the risk of an immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is off the table.\par \par \uc2 Adam Cole, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in London, said the company's model suggests the probability of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is as high as 33%, and this could jump to 45%, closer to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  danger zone than generally perceived, if next week's BOJ Tankan survey shows a key gauge of confidence among Japanese manufacturers tumbles due to deterioration in exports.\par \par \uc2 (Min Zeng writes about the Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for Dow Jones Newswires. He can be reached at 201-938-2096 or min.zeng@dowjones.com.)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 12-12-08 1613ET ]\par \par \uc2 1141   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020081212e4cc00042\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
