\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: BOJ Gov:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Way To Respond To Volatile  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2008\par 09:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Calling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "one possible response" to rapid swings in the yen's value, Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa Wednesday warned against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility, pushing the U.S. dollar higher against the Japanese unit.\par \par \uc2 The unexpected remark from the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to threaten an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets underlines how worried Japanese authorities are about the strength in the yen. Such comments are also rare from key BOJ officials as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls under the jurisdiction of the Finance Ministry.\par \par \uc2 "If moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market become too excessive, an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one way" to control high volatility, Shirakawa told a committee of the Upper House of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Parliament.\par \par \uc2 While the government hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 2004, market players have recently speculated that Japanese monetary authorities may make a move to prop up the greenback against the yen if it falls below Y90.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ governor's remarks helped to push the dollar temporarily higher against the yen. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose a little less than a third of a yen to Y92.90 before falling back. Around 0800 GMT, the dollar stood at Y92.50 on EBS.\par \par \uc2 "The yen is strengthening because markets seem to have bigger worries about the European and the U.S economies than they do about Japan's," Shirakawa said.\par \par \uc2 He added that the yen's strength since this summer versus the euro and dollar is a result of growing concerns about the global economic slowdown and turmoil in the financial markets stemming from the credit crunch.\par \par \uc2 Unwinding of yen carry trades - a tactic that involves borrowing cheap yen to invest overseas in assets with higher returns - is another cause of recent moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he said.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa acknowledged that conditions are becoming severe in the Japanese economy.\par \par \uc2 "The economy is stagnant due to drops in exports and high commodities prices," he said.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2935; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com \par    (Megumi Fujikawa contributed to this story.) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-12-08 0806GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081210e4ca000j0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
