\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Half of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  firms want  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  if yen jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 761 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2008\par 04:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * 46% of firms want \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent dlr below Y90\par \par \uc2  * 16% don't want \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 39% have no preference\par \par \uc2  * 65% think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if dlr falls to Y90 or below\par \par \uc2  * Among such firms, many expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Y90-85\par \par \uc2  By Akiko Takeda\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Nearly half of major Japanese firms want authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yen from rising beyond 90 yen to the dollar, to support Japan's export-driven economy, a Reuters survey showed.\par \par \uc2  The yen hit a 13-year high of 90.87 yen to the dollar in October, and traders say it may climb past such a level in coming months, as investors continue to shun risky carry trades due to credit market turmoil and fears of a global recession.\par \par \uc2  "A recovery of the export industry's earnings is important for the Japanese economy at this stage," said a company in the services sector.\par \par \uc2  Japan slid into its first recession in seven years in the third quarter as exports crumbled.\par \par \uc2  Exporters have been the main engine of growth for Japan's economy, but data released last week showed that manufacturers have forecast their biggest ever quarterly fall in output in the fourth quarter, fuelling worries of a deep recession.\par \par \uc2  The yen's historic jump in October was partly due to the unwinding of carry trades, in which investors sell low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the yen to fund investment in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assets.\par \par \uc2  Asked whether they wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the dollar from falling below 90 yen, 97 out of 213 major firms that responded, or 46 percent, said they hoped for such action from Japanese authorities.\par \par \uc2  Sixteen percent, or 34 respondents, said they did not want \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  while 39 percent, or 82 respondents, said they did not have a preferance.\par \par \uc2  In a separate query on the chances of yen-selling action by Japanese authorities, 65 percent of respondents said they thought \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar fell to 90 yen or below, while 35 percent said they were not expecting any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Among companies that expect such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 44 percent said they thought there would be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar falls below 90 yen, 29 percent said a dollar slide below 87.50 yen would trigger such action, and the remaining 27 percent thought Japan would wait until the dollar falls below 85 yen.\par \par \uc2  Some respondents said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves should generally be left to market forces, but added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be needed to curb sharp fluctuations.\par \par \uc2  "Trying to avert sharp swings may be necessary, but it would be better to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if possible," said a company in the oil, coal and ceramics industry.\par \par \uc2  Others were sceptical that solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities would be effective, and some questioned whether \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the right response to the turmoil in markets and the global economy.\par \par \uc2  But a transportation machinery maker, which said it wanted authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the dollar from falling below 90 yen, added that the biggest worry was how long the adverse economic conditions stemming from the financial crisis would last.\par \par \uc2  "Once we escape this situation, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions are likely to return to natural levels. In other words, the concern here is the time required to shake free from this situation, and this is not an issue that can be resolved through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the company said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stayed out the market for more than four years, the longest such stretch in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data going back to 1991.\par \par \uc2  Japan sold 35 trillion yen in the 15 months to March 2004 on concerns that excessive yen strength could dampen overseas demand for Japanese exports and hurt the economy.\par \par \uc2  The following is a table of the survey results: DO YOU WANT \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO PREVENT THE YEN FROM RISING BEYOND 90 YEN TO THE DOLLAR? (Percentage followed by number of responses)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      YES          NO       NO PREFERENCE\par -----------------------------------------------------------\par Total 213 responses:   46% (97)    16% (34)      39% (82)\par DO YOU THINK JAPANESE AUTHORITIES WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF THE\par DOLLAR FALLS TO 90 YEN OR BELOW?\par                      YES          NO\par -----------------------------------------------------------\par  Total 217 responses:  65% (142)   35% (75)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WHERE DO YOU EXPECT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SELL THE YEN VS\par THE DOLLAR?\par (Total 139 responses)\par Y90-Y87.50  Y87.50-Y85  Y85-Y82.50  Y82.50-Y80  BELOW Y80\par -----------------------------------------------------------\par   44% (61)   29% (40)     21% (29)    2% (3)      4% (6)\par  (Writing by Masayuki Kitano; Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL/JAPAN-YEN (POLL)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081202e4c200057\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
