\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2008\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: YOSANO: JAPAN INTEREST RATES AND YEN NOT LINKED NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano said Tuesday he doesn't think lower interest rates in Japan will prevent the yen from rising, suggesting that a rate cut now by the Bank of Japan wouldn't have much effect in boosting the economy. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AXA NZ FREEZES NZ$225M ON DEPOSIT GUARANTEE WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fund manager AXA New Zealand Tuesday said it is freezing NZ$225 million from three of its mortgage funds owing to an expected increase in redemptions because of uncertainty caused by a government deposit guarantee plan. (published 0214 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA BUSINESS CONDITIONS DN 11 PTS TO -4 IN 3Q-NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business conditions deteriorated sharply in the third quarter as sales and profits slumped, according to a quarterly survey by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  released Tuesday. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA FIN MIN: BUDGET SIGNIFICANTLY AFFECTED BY CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Finance Minister Lindsay Tanner said Tuesday the government's fiscal position will take a significant hit as the global financial crisis takes the shine off Australia's once buoyant economy. (published 2123 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS LIKELY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO EASE USD/SGD RISE-TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to ease the U.S. dollar's rise against the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , three traders said Tuesday. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NAKAGAWA: WOULDN'T COMMENT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa on Tuesday reiterated that sharp \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements aren't helpful to any nation, but he wouldn't say whether the government is close to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yen's rise. (published 0132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM OCT PRELIMINARY INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT +15.4% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's industrial production rose 15.4% on year this month on strong demand for cement, trucks and consumer goods, according to preliminary data published Tuesday by the General Statistics Office. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =S&P CUTS RATINGS ON ANOTHER $84.1B IN ALT-A RMBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services lowered its ratings on $84.1 billion of residential mortgage-backed securities transactions backed by Alt-A mortgage loans issued in 2006 and 2007, noting that most of the deals are backed by homes worth less than the amount of the loans. (published 2105 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BOE: SEES 'ENCOURAGING' SIGNS OF STABILIZATION IN BK FUNDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England said Tuesday that while the financial system remains "under strain" amid an accelerating economic downturn, recent measures taken by the authorities have had an encouraging impact on conditions. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA APPOINTS PBOC YI, STATISTICS HEAD MA TO PBOC POLICY BD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's State Council, the Cabinet, has appointed Yi Gang, a vice governor of the People's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and Ma Jiantang, director of the National Bureau of Statistics, to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy board, the PBOC said on its Web site. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA BANK REGULATOR CALLS FOR STRICTER FINANCIAL OVERSIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A top Chinese bank regulator called for stricter financial oversight, saying China ought to be mindful of the risks from lax financial-market supervision. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =COMMERCIAL PAPER MKT STILL STRAINED AFTER FED LAUNCHES FACILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve kicked off its much awaited commercial paper lending program Monday aimed at jump-starting the $1.45 trillion market for short-term lending, but investors say it could take days or weeks before short-term financing for U.S. companies loosens up. (published 2006 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(10/28) INDIAN MIDDLE CLASS GETS CAUGHT IN THE WHIRLWIND OF CREDIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The consumerism that has helped drive India's surging economy in recent years is showing its dark side, as overextended Indian credit-card holders get their first taste of delinquency and deep debt. (published 2351 GMT) [ 28-10-08 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081028e4as0003s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
