\par\par \b \uc2 TAKE A LOOK-Stocks soar, yen slumps\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2008\par 23:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks surged more than 10 percent on Tuesday, capping a worldwide rally in equity markets, as investors snapped up shares that had plunged during the worst October on record, and the yen posted its biggest decline against the dollar in more than 30 years.\par \par \uc2 The late-day U.S. surge also pulled up equity markets in Brazil and Mexico by double-digit percentage gains, and extended a plunge in benchmark U.S. government debt prices. The Dow industrials and the S&P 500 had their second-biggest point gains after the record rally two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 A Japanese newspaper report saying the Bank of Japan is considering an interest rate cut sparked the dollar-denominated Nikkei 225 futures index <NKc1> to jump 14 percent and hit an upward limit threshold, and helped ignite the U.S. rally.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve on Wednesday will cut interest rates at the end of its two-day policy meeting and central banks in Europe and Britain will likely follow next week also helped drive the rally in stocks, after they had sunk to 5-1/2-year lows. To read more, double-click on the square brackets below:\par \par \uc2 ---------------------------------------------------------------- MARKET REPORTS: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par > GLOBAL MARKETS-Stocks soar, yen slumps                      [ID:nN28417129]\par > MONEY MARKETS-Interbank funding costs ease, Fed frees CP   [ID:nN28416648]\par > EMERGING MARKETS-Assets rally on bargain hunting            [ID:nN28416684]\par   CREDIT CRISIS NEWS DRIVING GLOBAL MARKETS\par > Hopes rise for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate cuts                       [ID:nLS110165]\par > US consumers gloomiest ever as home prices plunge          