\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 27\b0\par\par\uc2 1,569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 08:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com. \par  \par    MACRO/\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 /FIXED INCOME: \par  \par =UPDATE: IN EMERGENCY STATEMENT, G7 WARNS AGAINST YEN RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance chiefs from the Group of Seven leading nations Monday issued an emergency statement warning investors against pushing up the yen too much, partly in response to Japan's pleas for help. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : YEN NOT BOWED BY G7 WARNING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Group of Seven statement warning about the recent strengthening of the yen failed to weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday amid skepticism that the major industrialized nations would conduct a joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF NAKAGAWA VOICES DISCONTENT OVER YEN RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister Monday used some of his strongest language yet to express his discontent with the yen's recent broad surges, adding to speculation that Tokyo may consider \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by itself. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KOREA CUTS RATE BY 75 BPS; BIGGEST CUT EVER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea slashed interest rates Monday, its second cut this month, in an emergency bid to prevent the ongoing financial market crisis from destroying the broader economy. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: RBA DEFENDS AUSTRALIAN DLR, RESTORES LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  has come off the sidelines to defend the Australian dollar, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets late Friday in Europe and then again in early Asia Monday. (published 0129 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA: MON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WITHIN HKD CONVERTIBILITY BAND VS USD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said strong demand for Hong Kong dollars prompted it to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday, though it reiterated the Hong Kong unit remains stable. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN SEP CSPI RISES AT SLOWEST PACE SINCE JAN 1985 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prices for corporate services in Japan grew at their slowest pace ever in September, reflecting the steep drop in commodity prices, data released by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  showed Monday. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NAKAGAWA: TO DECIDE WHAT GOVT WILL REQUEST OF BOJ BY NEXT MTG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa said Monday the government will decide what it will request of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  by its next policy meeting Friday. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN NAKAGAWA:ORDERED BY ASO TO EASE BKS' CAP ADEQUACY RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Shoichi Nakagawa said Monday he had received instructions from Prime Minister Taro Aso to take steps to tackle the volatile financial markets, including measures to shore up banks' capital bases. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: KOREA, CHINA TO REACH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SWAP DEAL SOON -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean and Chinese central banks will soon reach an agreement on a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap deal, Yonhap Infomax reported Monday, citing Deputy Minister of Strategy and Finance for International Affairs Shin Je-yoon. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ TO ACCEPT ASSET-BACKED COMML PAPER AS COLLATERAL FROM TUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it will accept as collateral asset-backed commercial paper guaranteed by the bank's counterparty financial institutions, starting Tuesday. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA PRES: TO PROVIDE PREEMPTIVE, SUFFICIENT LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's President Lee Myung-bak said Monday that the government will decisively and preemptively provide sufficient liquidity to help ease the domestic economy's woes due to the global financial turmoil. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BANK OF KOREA EASES LIMITS ON FOREIGN-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LOANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Monday it has eased limits on loans to South Korean exporters, especially those which had massive losses due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives contracts recently on a continued slide in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA: PUBLIC SECTOR LIQUIDITY NEEDED IN CRISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Research from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  released Monday supports public sector actions to provide liquidity in times of financial crisis. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA CANCELS TREASURY BOND TENDER DUE WEDNESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian Office of Financial Management Monday said it has canceled its A$450 million June 15, 2014 government bond tender scheduled for Wednesday due to a fall in demand for the securities. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA TO HOLD EXTRA SBI AUCTION LATER MON - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia will later Monday auction one-, three- and six month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia paper on top of the regular auction every Wednesday, an official said. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES REJECTS ALL BIDS FOR 91-DAY, 364-DAY TSY BILLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines on Monday rejected all bids for treasury bills at an auction, refusing banks' demand for higher yields amid intensifying risk aversion. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    EQUITIES: \par  \par  \par =3RD UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES SLUMP IN SKITTISH TRADE; HSI DN 9% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian share markets were sharply lower Monday with caution pervading emerging markets in particular as clouds gathered over the global economy. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =AUSTRALIA BANKS MAY NOT RUSH TO USE GOVT FUNDING GUARANTEE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eagerly awaited details of the Australian government's wholesale funding and deposit guarantee have been met with a muted response by market players, who say it won't likely result in a rush by banks to issue debt anytime soon. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CBA'S COLONIAL FIRST STATE FREEZES A$3.3B IN MORTGAGE FUNDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Colonial First State, the funds management arm of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Monday it has frozen withdrawals from some of its mortgage funds following similar moves by rivals in the wake of the government's decision to guarantee bank deposits. (published 0102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HERALD RESOURCES SEEKING BUYERS FOR DAIRI STAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Herald Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it is seeking expressions of interest for the potential sale of a stake of up to 29% in its Dairi zinc/lead project in Northern Sumatra. (published 0035 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NOBLE TO REPORT HIGHEST EVER OPERATING PROFIT IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodities supplier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Noble Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (N21.SG) said Monday that its third quarter operating profit will be the highest ever after the company's stock fell last week to an eight-year low on concerns over lower commodity demand amid the global slowdown. (published 0333 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAMES PACKER STANDS DOWN FROM PBL MEDIA BD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consolidated Media Ltd. said Monday that billionaire James Packer has stepped down from the board of the group's 25%-owned PBL Media unit, ending the Packer family's long association with the media assets. (published 0013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:STATE BANK OF INDIA 2Q NET +40% ON INTEREST INCOME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's largest bank by assets, \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday its unconsolidated net profit for the fiscal second quarter rose 40% from a year earlier, driven by rising interest income and other income. (published 0603 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BANCO DE ORO 3Q NET LOSS PHP1.3B ON LEHMAN> BDO.PH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banco de Oro Unibank Inc. said Monday it booked a PHP1.3 billion net loss in the third quarter due to exposure to collapsed U.S. investment bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0144 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA PACIFIC SWINGS TO 3Q NET LOSS ON INVEST LOSSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Pacific Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the country's third-largest life insurer by market share, said Monday it swung to a net loss in the third quarter from a net profit a year earlier on large investment losses and lower revenue. (published 0112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: KRISPY KREME HK APPOINTS ADVISER; MAY LIQUIDATE OPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong franchisee of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Krispy Kreme Doughnuts Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has appointed Briscoe & Wong Ltd. as its financial adviser for a potential liquidation if it can't find a buyer for the business, the adviser said Monday. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: KT FREETEL 3Q NET +17% ON DATA SALES, COST CONTROL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KT Freetel Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said third-quarter net profit rose 17% from a year earlier as it attracted more subscribers to lucrative data services and controlled marketing spending. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HYUNDAI MOBIS TO INVEST KRW100B IN HYBRID CAR PARTS BY 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Mobis Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it will invest KRW100 billion to develop key hybrid car parts by 2012 for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Automotive Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CRT RULES IN FAVOR OF LG VS WHIRLPOOL IN PATENT CASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said a U.S. federal court has ruled in favor of LG in a patent dispute with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Whirlpool Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NIPPON YUSEN JUL-SEP GROUP NET PROFIT Y46.9B VS Y26.3B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nippon Yusen K.K\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its revenue and profit for the July-September quarter grew sharply on year, thanks to continued strength in bulk shipping rates. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par LAFOOCO Q3 NET DOWN 66% TO VND4 BLN >LAF.VH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Long An Food Processing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lafooco\f28 \uc2 \f2 , recorded a 66% on-year fall in net profit to VND4 billion in the third quarter ended Sept. 30, local media said Monday. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ENERGY/COMMODITIES: \par  \par =UPDATE: GLOBAL FINCL CRISIS HITS NEW CALEDONIA NICKEL PROJ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Caledonia's government-backed nickel miner La Societe Miniere du Sud Pacifique has run into trouble with US$500 million of funding for the US$3.8 billion Koniambo nickel project, which it is developing with Anglo-Swiss miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MORE CHINESE STEEL PRODUCTION CUTS AHEAD -MACQUARIE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese steel mills are planning further production cuts because of a lack of export orders, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0334 GMT) [ 27-10-08 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081027e4ar000gm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
