\par\par \b \uc2 TOPWRAP 12-More US banks turn to Treasury; G7 sounds yen alarm\b0\par\par\uc2 1,146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 23:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Late session sell-off wipes out Wall Street rally\par \par \uc2 * SunTrust, other banks sell stakes to U.S. Treasury\par \par \uc2 * G7 warns soaring yen poses threat to stability\par \par \uc2 * ECB's Trichet says rate cut may come next week (For full crisis coverage, double click on [nCRISIS])\par \par \uc2 By Emily Kaiser\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 27 (Reuters) - More U.S. banks lined up for government cash on Monday and the Group of Seven expressed concern that Japan's soaring yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  posed a threat to financial and economic stability as recession worries spread worldwide.\par \par \uc2 Stock markets worldwide also tumbled again with key Wall Street indexes hitting a 5-1/2-year low.\par \par \uc2 Officials in Europe and Asia took emergency actions on Monday to shore up their financial positions. South Korea cut interest rates, Australia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the International Monetary Fund moved to help Hungary and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The credit crisis, which began with failing U.S. mortgages, has mushroomed into a worldwide rout as investors dump stocks and commodities, shun higher-risk emerging markets and seek out the safest government bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yet, promising signs emerged that government efforts to revive credit markets were beginning to pay off.\par \par \uc2 London interbank lending rates moderated and the U.S. Federal Reserve set the terms for its program to buy commercial paper, bolstering a market that is vital for funding companies' day-to-day business activities. For full story, see [ID:nN27310396]\par \par \uc2 In the U.S. housing market, one of the sources of the global crisis, sales of newly constructed single-family homes rose in September and inventories shrank, as builders slashed prices to their lowest level in four years. [ID:nN27319783]\par \par \uc2 But U.S. stocks failed to sustain a midday rally as the Dow Jones industrials <.DJI> and S&P 500 <.SPX> fell to 5-1/2-year lows. Japan's Nikkei <.N225> tumbled 6.4 percent to its lowest close in 26 years and Europe's FTSEurofirst 300 <.FTEU3> fell 1.7 percent to a 5-1/2-year closing low.\par \par \uc2 "It is so negative out there, you felt like a skater without any skates -- it couldn't stay up," said Angel Mata, managing director of listed equity trading at \uc2 Stifel Nicolaus\uc2  Capital in Baltimore.\par \par \uc2 "People right now are expecting the worst -- a total collapse of the hedge fund industry with half of them (hedge funds) not existing anymore. Moms and pops with 401(k)s are saying, 'I have had enough and don't want to be in there any more,'" Mata said.\par \par \uc2 Financial companies including \uc2 Comerica Inc\uc2  , \uc2 SunTrust Banks Inc\uc2  and \uc2 State Street Corp\uc2  agreed to sell stakes to the U.S. Treasury Department in exchange for cash infusions -- part of the $700 billion rescue plan approved by Congress earlier this month. [ID:nN27303243]\par \par \uc2 The U.S. government was also considering at least $5 billion in aid to facilitate a merger between hobbled auto makers \uc2 General Motors Corp\uc2  and \uc2 Chrysler LLC\uc2 , according to a source familiar with Treasury's thinking. [ID:nN27331921]\par \par \uc2 Loews Corp\uc2  , a conglomerate run by the billionaire Tisch family, said it would inject up to $1.25 billion in new capital into its \uc2 CNA Financial Corp\uc2  commercial insurance unit after bad investments drove up losses. [ID:nN2726821]\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to trim short-term interest rates at its policy-setting meeting later in the week, and British Prime Minister Gordon Brown hinted that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action may be widespread. [ID:nN27320203]\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said a rate cut next week was a possibility, though not a certainty. [ID:nLR497994]\par \par \uc2 MSCI's main world stock index <.MIWD00000PUS> dropped 4.3 percent, putting its year-to-date decline near 50 percent. Its emerging market counterpart <.MSCIEF> lost 4.1 percent, and earlier hit a four-year low.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices earlier slipped below $63 per barrel, less than half the record high above $147 notched in July.\par \par \uc2 With financial markets in turmoil, the U.S. presidential election has focused on the economy, which has helped to push Democratic candidate Barack Obama ahead of Republican John McCain in opinion polls.\par \par \uc2 The election is next Tuesday, Nov. 4.\par \par \uc2 COOLING THE YEN\par \par \uc2 Volatility has surged across financial markets as investors are forced to sell assets -- often bought with borrowed money -- to repay creditors or cover margin calls as asset prices fall and credit limits are breached.\par \par \uc2 The upheaval has also hit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 A brief G7 statement focused on the yen, fanning speculation the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in four years.\par \par \uc2 "We are concerned about the recent excessive volatility in the exchange rate of the yen and its possible adverse implications for economic and financial stability," said the group, which includes the United States, Japan, Germany, Britain, France, Italy and Canada.\par \par \uc2 The yen's rapid ascent against the dollar and euro is making Japanese exports much more expensive at a time when its overseas customers lurch toward recession. [ID:nT78987]\par \par \uc2 The dollar, however, rose against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , except the yen, so there was skepticism about whether any coordinated action on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forthcoming. <.DXY> [FRX/]\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying Australian dollars for U.S. dollars in Europe.\par \par \uc2 FOR RICHER OR POORER\par \par \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group Inc\uc2  , Japan's biggest bank, said it would raise up to $10.6 billion to replenish a capital base depleted by plunging stocks and its investment in \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  . [ID:nT13538]\par \par \uc2 In South Korea, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resorted to a record interest rate cut as it grapples with the crisis that has shattered investor confidence and threatened a deep recession.\par \par \uc2 The 15-month-old crisis also continued to take a toll on emerging markets as investors withdrew funds and commodity exporters faced falling prices for everything from corn to copper.\par \par \uc2 The IMF said it reached an agreement with Hungary to provide a "substantial financing package" in the next few days that would include funding by the European Union and some individual European governments. [ID:nN26287887]\par \par \uc2 It agreed on a $16.5 billion loan for Ukraine on Sunday and last week unveiled a $2.1 billion package for Iceland.\par \par \uc2 In an effort to ease credit strains, the IMF's board is expected on Friday to consider a liquidity swap fund that would provide a group of pre-approved advanced emerging economies with short-term financing carrying few or no conditions. (Additional writing and reporting by Claudia Parsons in New York, Jeremy Gaunt in London and Kevin Plumberg in Hong Kong; Editing by Steve Orlofsky, Brian Moss, Philip Barbara, Jeffrey Benkoe, Gary Crosse)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL/ (TOPWRAP 12, PIX)|LANGEN|G|RBN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|CANT|AUF|Z|J|UKI|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081027e4ar000w7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
