\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -US dollar, yen uptrend intact as risky assets shunned\b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 06:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen near 13-year peaks vs dollar despite G7 warning\par \par \uc2 * Dollar gains vs euro, sterling\par \par \uc2 * Markets on alert for BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The dollar and yen advanced on Monday as fears of global recession prompted investors to abandon risky assets, boosting both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that were sold to finance these investments.\par \par \uc2 The yen hovered near 13-year peaks against the dollar and rose to its highest since 2002 versus the euro, despite a statement from the Group of Seven finance officials expressing concern about excessive volatility in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar climbed to its strongest level against the single euro zone \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in about 2-1/2 years.\par \par \uc2 The G7 major industrialized nations said they would continue to monitor markets closely, and cooperate as appropriate, raising prospects for a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The whole deleveraging dynamic playing out is accompanied by a reversal in carry trades," said Jack Crooks, president of Black Swan Capital in Palm City, Florida.\par \par \uc2 "Both the dollar and the yen, which sport the two lowest yields among major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are the biggest beneficiaries of global capital flows right now. Jumping in front of (these two) is like jumping in front of a freight train -- it simply doesn't stop."\par \par \uc2 The yen, which has risen roughly 20 percent on a trade-weighted basis this month, has gained as investors unwound carry trades, which used the low-yielding yen to buy everything from higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stocks and commodities. These trades have collapsed in recent weeks as market players have been forced to sell assets to raise cash.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was also a beneficiary of global deleveraging. Investors had used dollar-denominated loans to pump up investments elsewhere. When the crisis escalated over the summer, borrowers began calling in these loans, resulting in a scramble for dollars.\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon New York trading, the dollar was hovering around 94.00 yen, pulling back after rising to about 94.48 yen after the G7 warning. On Friday, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had slid to a 13-year low of 90.95, according to electronic trading platform EBS.\par \par \uc2 YEN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  MAY BE LESS EFFECTIVE\par \par \uc2 The euro rebounded somewhat to 117.68 yen as U.S. stocks repaired morning weakness, after it hit a 6-1/2-year low of 113.62 during earlier trade, EBS data show.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the G7 warning has fallen on deaf ears, as investors continued to snap up the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the Nikkei stock index plunged over 6 percent.\par \par \uc2 French Finance Minister Christine Lagarde said on Monday any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the yen will be a purely \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertaking.\par \par \uc2 "Chances of a successful yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are weak as long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains boosted by capital (returning) to the yen," said Ashraf Laidi, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CMC Markets USA in New York.\par \par \uc2 He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would also be futile as Japanese investors, who in the past had embarked on foreign equity buying, have turned risk averse, with the 26-year low in the Nikkei wiping out much of their wealth.\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the euro was also a little firmer in afternoon trade around $1.2544. Earlier, it fell to a 2-1/2-year low at $1.2335. The euro had been hurt by comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet saying the bank could cut rates at its next meeting on Nov. 6. The ECB has cut rates by 50 basis points together with other central banks early this month.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market buying Aussie dollars and selling the greenback in Europe on Monday, traders said. It also confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday and in Asian trade earlier in the global session to stabilize the flagging Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar fell to a 6-1/2-year low at US$0.6025, according to Reuters data. It was last at US$0.6090. Against the yen, the Aussie was at 57.23 yen after sinking to 55.11 yen on Friday, the lowest since it was allowed to trade freely in December 1983. (Editing by Toni Reinhold)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 7)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081027e4ar0001k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
