\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Confirms It Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt In August\b0\par\par\uc2 143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2008\par 12:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities didn't take any action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The MOF said it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from July 30 to Aug. 27, as expected by market participants.\par \par \uc2 Japan has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since March 2004, when it abruptly ended a 15-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in which it sold Y35 trillion, mostly for dollars, in a bid to keep a stronger yen from snuffing out an economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data covered trades that are settled in August. Trades in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market are settled after two business days.\par \par \uc2 -By Tomoyuki Tachikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com [ 29-08-08 1005GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080829e48t000in\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
