\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Plan Doesn't Scare Traders\b0\par\par\uc2 By Riva Froymovich   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2008\par 21:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are brushing off a news report that authorities in the U.S., Europe and Japan agreed back in March on a contingency plan to boost the dollar through joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Authorities typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when markets are disorderly - a distinct possibility when the parties convened in March, given the plunging dollar, a run on a major bank and low market liquidity. But discussion is far from action, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "They seemed to have coordinated a whole lot to choose not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ray Farris, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in London, who added that the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  always exists.\par \par \uc2 Japanese daily The Nikkei reported in its Thursday morning edition that the U.S. Treasury Department, Japan's Finance Ministry and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considered issuing an emergency statement in support of the dollar at a March 15-16 meeting through the Group of Seven industrialized nations. Citing unnamed sources, the report said authorities outlined a coordinated dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but did not set a specific exchange rate for initiating action. The three leading economies haven't jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 2000.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said they wouldn't be surprised if such talks took place. That weekend, the Treasury and the Federal Reserve engineered the takeover of investment-bank \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  by \uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\uc2 . (JPM) in a move aimed at stabilizing the financial system. It was also a time when the dollar was hitting multi-year lows daily against its major trading rivals.\par \par \uc2 "One can probably be reasonably confident that Japanese and European policy makers had been knocking at the Treasury's door with concerns and complaints regarding the dollar's fall long before this particular meeting," said Sacha Tihanyi, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 But after that mid-March weekend, the dollar remained weak and eventually fell to a new record low against the euro, which rose above $1.6000 last month from a previous high of $1.5905 struck on March 17. However, the dollar did bottom out versus the yen at Y95.77 that Monday.\par \par \uc2 Divergent Path Of Monetary Policy\par \par \uc2 Yet, while the timing might make sense, other factors make an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan seem unlikely.\par \par \uc2 Exchange rates back in March reflected the divergent paths of monetary policy in the U.S. and the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. at that time wanted the dollar to stay weak to help boost its exports - the economy's savior during the credit crunch. The Fed had already shaved 2.25 percentage points off its lending rate and was gearing up for another three-quarter-percentage-point cut on March 18. Fed funds are currently at 2.0%.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, was already concerned about inflation pressures although it didn't raise rates until July - by a quarter point to 4.25%.\par \par \uc2 "We've been arguing for quite some time that we did not see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. and the euro zone) as a likely event due to the different focuses of monetary policy," said Kasper Kirkegaard, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  in Copenhagen.\par \par \uc2 Though the Nikkei report said that renewed dollar weakness could rekindle discussions of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market conditions have changed since last March. While credit conditions remain tight and the U.S. banking sector is still struggling, weakness is now spreading around the globe. As a result, the dollar has staged a significant recovery from its record low and was recently trading Thursday at $1.4700 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 With the dollar's turn in fortune, the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has faded.\par \par \uc2 "President (George W.) Bush is still set to be the first American president since at least the break up of Bretton Woods that has not authorized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market, and given the recent price action, the distinction looks relatively safe," said Marc Chandler, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 (Riva Froymovich reports on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for Dow Jones Newswires in New York. The writer can be reached at 201-938-5063 or by e-mail: riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 08-28-08 1545ET ]\par \par \uc2 1141   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080828e48s0006g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
