\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-US, Europe, Japan discussed dlr rescue in March-source\b0\par\par\uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2008\par 03:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 28 (Reuters) - The United States, Europe, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March discussed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rescue the dollar if it extended sharp losses it was suffering at the time, an international finance source familiar with the talks told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on condition of anonymity, the source also said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities from the three regions were in close contact in March. No \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted.\par \par \uc2 The source was contacted to comment on a Nikkei newspaper report which said joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar was planned when it was plunging in March at the time of U.S. investment bank \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2 ' collapse.\par \par \uc2 Officials from the U.S. Treasury Department, Japan's Finance Ministry and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly drew up a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contingency plan over the weekend of March 15-16, the Nikkei said, citing sources familiar with the situation.\par \par \uc2 The officials did not specify levels for initiating the dollar rescue plan, but in the event of a free-fall, they agreed to coordinate aggressive buying of the greenback and sell yen <JPY=> and euros <EUR=>, the newspaper said.\par \par \uc2 No coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place as the dollar began to recover shortly after the U.S. authorities brokered \uc2 JP Morgan Chase\uc2 's buyout of \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  -- the biggest victim so far in the year-old credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 As measured by the dollar index <.DXY>, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged to that record low on March 17, the first market day after the announcement of the \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  deal, but it later recovered.\par \par \uc2 The dollar tumbled to a 13-year low of 95.77 yen that day but is now near 109 yen.\par \par \uc2 A U.S. Treasury spokeswoman, the Federal Reserve and the ECB declined to comment on the Nikkei report. Japan's top financial diplomat, Naoyuki Shinohara, also said he had no comment.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Bunmei Ibuki told Reuters the nation's monetary authorities will decide how to deal with any sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in the future based on economic fundamentals at the time.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said even though a rescue never took place, any such agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be important in the future if the dollar were to tumble again, or other exchange rates to move very sharply.\par \par \uc2 "If downside risks to the dollar emerge from here on, the market will keep in mind the possibility of similar action by authorities," said Takahide Nagasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Daiwa Securities SMBC.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei report had little immediate impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since the dollar has already rebounded 10 percent from a record low it struck against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "The report would have had a huge psychological impact if it had come out when the dollar was trading around 100 yen," said Tomoko Fujii, head of economics and strategy for Japan at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The United States, Europe and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since September 2000, when they acted to prop up a sliding euro. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in March 2004.\par \par \uc2 Even as the dollar slid after the flare-up of the credit market turmoil last August, there had been a perception among market players that U.S. authorities were willing to tolerate falls in the dollar in a policy of 'benign neglect', to help support U.S. exports as the economy faltered.\par \par \uc2 But market players detected a shift in U.S. officials' stance towards the dollar in June when Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke issued a rare warning on the inflation risk posed by a weak dollar, and Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson declined to rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  framework, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to supply yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps. The plan also called for using a previously established swap mechanism between the United States and Europe.\par \par \uc2 "If anything, the fact that officials recognised the concern about the dollar's decline seems somewhat supportive for the dollar as maybe benign neglect was not so neglectful," said Marc Chandler, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "At the end of the day, however, President Bush is still set to be the first American president since at least the break-up of Bretton Woods (who) has not authorised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and given the recent price action the distinction looks relatively safe." (Reporting by Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss in New York; Leika Kihara and Masayuki Kitano in Tokyo; Editing by Michael Watson and Swaha Pattanaik)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NIKKEI (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|J|Z|NAT|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080828e48s0001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
