\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves $1.002 trln at end-June\b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2008\par 01:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP]) (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 7 (Reuters) - Japan's foreign reserves hit $1.002 trillion at the end of June, logging the first rise in three months thanks in part to investment returns and the euro's rise versus the dollar that inflated the value of euro-denominated bonds in the stockpile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. [JPRES=ECI]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Higher gold prices also helped lift Japan's reserves -- the\par world's second largest after China's -- back above $1 trillion,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 but still shy of the record high of $1.016 trillion at the end of March, a ministry official said on Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro <EUR=> edged up to $1.5754 at the end of June from $1.5559 at the end of May, while the benchmark gold price rose to $930.25 an ounce at the end of June from $885.75 the month before.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ministry, which is in charge of Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, does not disclose the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  breakdown of Japan's reserves, but most is in U.S. dollars as past \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has taken the form of dollar buying.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's foreign reserves ballooned after massive yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2003 and early 2004 as Tokyo tried to stem a rapid rise in the yen from derailing a fragile economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo has kept out of the market since then, but the income on the reserves has crept up steadily.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The massive reserves have stirred a debate among Japanese lawmakers about whether Japan should follow countries like China into launching a sovereign wealth fund to invest some of the cash pile. But the finance ministry remains cautious about the idea.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ministry started operating a new section within its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets division on Friday that will focus on managing Japan's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. [ID:nT343958]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But ministry officials have said the launch of the new section does not mean Japan will start investing the stockpile more actively into risky assets to seek higher returns. JAPAN OFFICIAL RESERVE ASSETS (in billion dollars)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                  END-JUNE          END-MAY          YEAR-AGO\par  TOTAL             1,001.549          996.975          913.572\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To view the full tables, go to the website of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mof.go.jp/english/e1c006.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mof.go.jp/english/e1c006.htm}}}\uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Chris Gallagher)\f28 \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|NAT|U|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080706e476000ks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
