\par\par \b \uc2 Japan MOF to start new section to manage  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2008\par 09:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 3 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will start operating a new section within its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets division on Friday that will focus on managing Japan's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 But ministry officials have said the launch of the new section does not mean Japan will start investing the stockpile more actively into risky assets to seek higher returns.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets remain sensitive to any sign of reserve policy changes by Japan, which holds around $1 trillion in foreign reserves -- the world's second largest after China.\par \par \uc2 "There is no change in our policy of prioritising liquidity and safety in managing reserves before pursuing profitability," a finance ministry official told Reuters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets division has 16 staff members, including those in charge of managing reserves and those monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements.\par \par \uc2 The creation of the new office will add two new staff to the existing reserve management team. The ministry had requested the reorganisation of the division under the state budget for the current fiscal year, which was approved earlier this year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves ballooned after massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003 and early 2004 as Tokyo tried to keep a rapid rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from derailing a fragile economic recovery and accelerating deflation.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo has kept out of the market since then, but the income on the reserves has crept up steadily.\par \par \uc2 The MOF, which is in charge of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, does not give \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakdowns of its external reserves.\par \par \uc2 But historical data on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has mostly taken the form of dollar buying, suggests most of Tokyo's hefty reserves are in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In recent years, the MOF has been diversifying the range of dollar-denominated assets in its foreign reserves and has also been buying and selling securities in the secondary market, using private brokerages, rather than simply buying new issues and holding them to maturity.\par \par \uc2 But the ministry remains cautious about more aggressive ways to manage its reserves, such as the idea of setting up a new investment body to seek bigger profits.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo does not hold stocks or real estate in its reserves and has no plan to divert its reserves out of dollars into euros, saying a top priority is to avoid distorting the market.\par \par \uc2 The ministry's guidelines for its reserves management says eligible assets include central government bonds, agency bonds, supranational bonds and securitised bonds that offer high liquidity and certainty of redemption, as well as deposits in foreign central banks and financial institutions at home and abroad with high credibility.\par \par \uc2 -- To view the MOF's guidelines for the management of foreign reserves, see the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  website:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mof.go.jp/english/if/050404.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mof.go.jp/english/if/050404.htm}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Yoko Nishikawa; Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/RESERVES|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|NAT|U|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080703e473000ks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
