\par\par \b \uc2 AT A GLANCE: ASEM Meeting Of Asia, Europe Ministers In Jeju\b0\par\par\uc2 1,048 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2008\par 14:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Finance ministers from Asia and Europe are meeting in Jeju, South Korea June 14-17. Following are Dow Jones' top stories from the event:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  =ASEM FIN MINS ECHO G8 IN WARNING OVER DANGERS OF INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Finance Ministers and representatives from Europe and Asia warned Monday that the world economy faces downside risks, notably from high inflation and the fallout of the U.S. subprime mortgage crisis. (published 1053 GMT)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  =UPDATE: JAPAN NUKAGA'S SILENCE SUGGESTS UNCLEAR ON YEN ROLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Japan's Finance Minister Monday once again declined to comment about whether Tokyo is favor of the U.S. policy of a stronger dollar, but he appears to have become more concerned about domestic inflationary pressures. (published 0101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JAPAN FIN MIN NUKAGA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOT DISCUSSED AT ASEM, G8 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga said Monday \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issues were not discussed at the Asia-Europe Meeting, or at the Group of Eight finance ministers gathering in Osaka last weekend. (published 0933 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASEM AGREE STEPS NEEDED TO COMBAT OIL MKT SPECULATION-KOREA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--South Korea's finance minister Kang Man-soo said Monday that speculation has been helping push up global oil prices. (published 0824 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: EU BAJUK: HIGHER ECB RATES WOULD NOT BE A CONCERN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is right to keep the markets guessing on whether it'll tighten monetary policy next month, and an increase in interest rates wouldn't be a matter for concern, Andrej Bajuk, chair of the Ecofin and Slovenia's finance minister, said Monday. (published 1028 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN NUKAGA: TO CHECK IF SPECULATION AFFECTS OIL,FOOD PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga said Monday that European and Asian counterparts will keep an eye on whether speculative moves are partly the cause of recent oil and food price rises. (published 0839 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA VICE FIN MIN:PRICES, SPECULATIVE CAPITAL KEY CHALLENGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea - Rising inflation and inflows of speculative capital are key challenges facing the world economy, especially the developing countries, Li Yong, a China vice finance minister, said Monday. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN: WORLD ECON FACES UNCERTAINTIES, DOWNSIDE RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--The world economy continues to face "uncertainties and downside risks", Japanese finance minister Fukushiro Nukaga said Monday. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE:FRENCH FIN MIN: INFLATION IS KEY ISSUE IN ASIA, EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Inflation is a key issue in both Asia and Europe, French finance minister Christine Lagarde said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In both regions, inflation resulting in particular from high prices of oil and food is a key problem," Lagarde said at a press conference. (published 0406GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ADB KURODA: COSTLY MATERIALS MAY NOT SPUR JAPAN'S INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Japan is not facing inflationary pressures for now and inflation won't cause the economy any real problems given the nation's ability to tolerate high crude oil and food prices, the president of the Asian Development Bank said Monday. (published 0341GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM HAS ITS OWN INFLATION WOES BUT IT CAN COPE -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Vietnam will have its "own difficulty" in dealing with higher prices in the short term even as the rest of the world grapples with the fallout of rising inflation, a senior Vietnamese finance official said Monday. (published 0256GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  =UPDATE: NUKAGA SILENT ON IF JAPAN SUPPORTS US \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Japan's Finance Minister Sunday remained mum about whether the country supports the U.S. policy of a stronger U.S. dollar, indicating Tokyo may not share Washington's anxiety over dollar weakness. (published 1052 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: FRANCE FIN MIN: WOULD BE GOOD IF JPY RISES VS EUR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--It would be very good if the yen could appreciate against the euro, French finance minister Christine Lagarde said Sunday. She made the comment after coming out of a bilateral meeting here with Japanese finance minister Fukushiro Nukaga. (published 1109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KOREA FIN MIN SAYS MANIPULATING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RATE UNDESIRABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--South Korea's finance minister Kang Man-soo said Sunday that it's "undesirable" to manipulate the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The minister said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate should be determined by market forces, and any government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't desirable, according to the official, who declined to be named. (published 0953 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA FIN MIN HINTS '08 6% GDP GROWTH TARGET LIKELY TO BE CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--South Korea's Minister of Strategy and Finance Kang Man-soo suggested Sunday that the government is set to cut its economic growth target of 6% in the wake of surging global oil prices. (published 0711 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN EX-MOF WATANABE HINTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ACTION STILL POSSIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--Japan's former Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs said Sunday the possibility of the U.S. and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets cannot be ruled out if the dollar falls sharply against the yen. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:WORLD FACES THREE CHALLENGES -FRANCE FINANCE MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--The French finance minister said Sunday that the world faces three closely interrelated challenges. "The so-called triple-F (challenges) consists of financial, fuel and food...and to fix one, we need to fix the others," Christine Lagarde, the French Minister for Economy, Industry and Employment, told Dow Jones Newswires on the sidelines of the Asia-Europe Meeting held in Jeju, South Korea. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECON SLOWDOWN, INFLATION CHINA'S KEY RISKS - EX-PBOC ADVISER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--A potential domestic economic slowdown, compounded by weakness in the U.S. economy, is among the "major challenges" China faces, a former adviser at the People's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Sunday. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: EU'S ALMUNIA: HAS NO POLICY TO PROMOTE USE OF EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JEJU, South Korea (Dow Jones)--The European Union has no policy to promote the use of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in global commerce, the European Commission's top economic official said Sunday. (published 1010 GMT) [ 16-06-08 1204GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080616e46g000mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
