\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar edges down ahead of G8 and inflation data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Satomi Noguchi   \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2008\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 13 (Reuters) - The dollar fell from a nearly four-month high against the yen on Friday, as investors booked profits from this week's rally before a gathering of Group of Eight finance ministers in Japan this weekend.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had staged broad gains this week after anti-inflation talk from Federal Reserve officials, and Thursday's surprisingly strong retail sales figures added to expectations for Fed interest rate increases this year.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses would be limited by investors' expectations for more dollar-supportive comments from U.S. Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson.\par \par \uc2 Paulson and other finance ministers from eight rich nations will discuss the global economy and soaring oil and food prices at a meeting to prepare for the G8 leaders' summit in July.\par \par \uc2 But others said the dollar looked a little overstretched and may face further profit-taking as investors have probably gone too far in pricing in the possibility of three Fed interest rate hikes this year.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar's rally against the yen looks as if it has run its course," said Hideki Amikura, a deputy general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section at Nomura Trust and Banking.\par \par \uc2 Amikura said the dollar may weaken further if Friday's U.S. data shows that a rise in consumer prices for May was smaller than expected and cools some expectations for Fed rate rises.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.2 percent against the yen from late U.S. trade on Thursday to 107.70 yen stepping back from a nearly four-month high of 108.08 yen hit the previous day.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan kept interest rates steady at 0.5 percent on Friday, as widely expected. Investors were interested in hearing BOJ Governor Masaaki Shirakawa's views on global inflation when he speaks at post-meeting news conference from 0630 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The euro edged up 0.1 percent to $1.5458 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been buffeted by comments from officials that suggested the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not about to embark on an extended period of monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 Market players were also closely watching the outcome of Ireland's referendum on the European Union reform treaty, with results expected on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The rejection of the EU constitution by France and the Netherlands in 2005 was one factor behind the euro's fall that year. But analysts are divided on whether the Irish vote will have much of an impact on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this time.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar jumped 0.4 percent to $0.9406 after Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens suggested a tight monetary policy remains essential for the country.\par \par \uc2 G8 WATCH\par \par \uc2 Paulson said earlier in the week he would never rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a potential policy tool to stem the dollar's slide.\par \par \uc2 His comments came just after Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke last week surprised the market with a rare warning that a weak dollar was adding to price pressures, signalling to investors a shift in Washington's view on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Market players will look for clues on whether the United States will back its words with action and whether other governments will support \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when G8 finance ministers gather on Saturday in Osaka, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The group comprises Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, the United States and Russia. (Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \uc2 LANGEN|GNN|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080613e46d000as\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
